WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.007
[theme song playing]

00:07.090 --> 00:09.885
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:11.637 --> 00:14.723
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:15.474 --> 00:20.479
♪ Deep in the silence
But it doesn't mean you're lost ♪

00:20.562 --> 00:24.274
♪ And I'll tell you what ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:27.236
♪ We're on the train ♪

00:27.319 --> 00:30.948
♪ I promise I'll be where you are ♪

00:31.865 --> 00:35.827
♪ If any thought is against you ♪

00:35.911 --> 00:39.540
♪ With you, I am starting over ♪

00:39.623 --> 00:43.669
♪ We're learning to walk again ♪

00:43.752 --> 00:44.670
[song concludes]

00:44.753 --> 00:45.963
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:46.713 --> 00:49.091
[soft pensive music playing]

00:49.174 --> 00:52.261
[Mi-rae in Korean] When Mi-ji's dream
was to own a stationery store,

00:52.344 --> 00:53.804
mine was to become a tree.

00:53.887 --> 00:55.597
- [nurse] Hello.
- [Ok-hui] Hi.

00:56.848 --> 00:58.267
[Ok-hui] The nurse is here.

00:59.059 --> 01:01.562
- [nurse] Time for her shot.
- [Ok-hui] Okay.

01:02.229 --> 01:03.647
She's getting the shot…

01:03.730 --> 01:05.357
- [nurse] Yes.
- …on her left arm, right?

01:05.440 --> 01:08.277
[Mi-rae] If I were a tree,
needles wouldn't hurt.

01:09.528 --> 01:11.092
- Why did I have to be sick…
- [groans]

01:11.192 --> 01:13.699
- [nurse] Her veins…
- [Mi-rae] …making everyone suffer…

01:13.782 --> 01:17.077
- Stop poking around and do it right.
- …feel sad and get mad?

01:17.160 --> 01:19.580
Mi-rae, are you okay? You did great.

01:19.663 --> 01:22.102
- You're okay, right?
- [Mi-rae] That's when I started

01:22.165 --> 01:23.125
pretending to be a tree…

01:23.208 --> 01:25.294
- Just a little pinch.
- …quietly enduring everything.

01:25.377 --> 01:26.545
[soft pensive music continues]

01:26.628 --> 01:28.630
[Mi-rae]
I couldn't do anything about the pain,

01:29.923 --> 01:32.843
but I could choose not to cry.

01:32.926 --> 01:35.762
[presenter] And with that,
we hereby present this award.

01:45.439 --> 01:47.065
[soft pensive music continues]

01:49.693 --> 01:50.736
[young Mi-rae exhales]

01:50.819 --> 01:52.529
[Mi-rae] I may not have stood out,

01:53.363 --> 01:55.365
but I knew how to endure.

01:58.327 --> 01:59.870
- [thunder rumbling]
- [rain pattering]

01:59.953 --> 02:00.871
[music fades]

02:00.954 --> 02:03.165
[Se-jin] Seriously? A blackout?

02:03.248 --> 02:05.000
Did you call home?

02:05.083 --> 02:07.544
I already told Mom
I wouldn't be home tonight.

02:09.296 --> 02:12.174
I wasn't planning to come here, though.

02:12.257 --> 02:15.594
[inhales deeply]
This is only going to fuel the rumors.

02:16.136 --> 02:17.429
We're screwed.

02:18.430 --> 02:19.473
Jeez.

02:21.683 --> 02:23.310
[inhales deeply]

02:23.393 --> 02:24.686
Seriously, why did you come?

02:25.562 --> 02:29.107
My friend said he could take me
anywhere I wanted,

02:29.191 --> 02:31.610
but this was the only place
I could think of.

02:32.486 --> 02:33.403
Why?

02:34.446 --> 02:36.490
Because what's out there is fake,

02:37.532 --> 02:39.034
and this place is real.

02:39.117 --> 02:40.035
At least to me.

02:43.747 --> 02:45.874
Then why do you hate the rumors so much?

02:47.959 --> 02:49.461
There's no reason to like them.

02:52.839 --> 02:54.007
I like them.

02:54.508 --> 02:55.676
The rumors about us.

02:55.759 --> 02:58.095
[soft tender music playing]

02:59.471 --> 03:02.307
[thunder crashing]

03:06.436 --> 03:07.813
[stomach growls]

03:09.773 --> 03:12.818
If you're hungry or cold, just say so.

03:12.901 --> 03:14.653
Why don't you ever say anything?

03:15.779 --> 03:17.322
How can you say nothing

03:17.406 --> 03:19.658
until your stomach
is growling like thunder?

03:21.702 --> 03:23.537
Noodles first?

03:23.620 --> 03:24.955
Or the seasoning?

03:25.497 --> 03:26.665
That is the question.

03:26.748 --> 03:28.709
For the record, I'm team seasoning.

03:29.209 --> 03:32.337
You have to put the toppings in first

03:32.421 --> 03:34.089
so the veggie flavors really seep in.

03:34.172 --> 03:37.384
They say you can put the noodles in
before the water boils.

03:37.467 --> 03:38.385
[quirky music playing]

03:38.468 --> 03:42.639
But dropping the noodles into cold water
just doesn't sit right with me.

03:43.181 --> 03:45.767
Your name is Han Se-jin?

03:45.851 --> 03:47.352
You didn't even know my name?

03:47.436 --> 03:48.437
Wait!

03:49.062 --> 03:51.690
I didn't collect those.
That was all my grandfather…

03:51.773 --> 03:54.693
You're the Han Se-jin
from Ihan Asset Management?

03:55.193 --> 03:56.319
How do you know me?

03:56.903 --> 03:58.405
Are you into stocks?

03:58.488 --> 04:02.409
There's even a novel based
on the public takeover bid for Hyudi Bio.

04:02.492 --> 04:05.036
And Yeongmin Steel?
You persuaded the minority shareholders

04:05.120 --> 04:07.664
and took over the company
with just a one percent margin.

04:07.748 --> 04:11.168
If that happened in a TV show,
people would say it's too far-fetched…

04:12.043 --> 04:13.628
[music concludes]

04:13.712 --> 04:14.755
What?

04:14.838 --> 04:17.632
So you're not quiet.
You just chose not to talk.

04:17.716 --> 04:19.634
How did you stay so quiet until now?

04:20.260 --> 04:22.095
I like this version of you.

04:22.179 --> 04:24.222
Don't stop now. Tell me more.

04:24.890 --> 04:26.808
Never mind.

04:26.892 --> 04:28.185
From the sound of it,

04:28.268 --> 04:30.479
you're more interested
in activist funds than me.

04:30.562 --> 04:33.440
"Interested" is an understatement.
My thesis was on shareholder activism--

04:33.523 --> 04:35.650
High school seniors
write thesis papers these days?

04:35.734 --> 04:37.235
[Mi-rae] No…

04:37.319 --> 04:38.403
I read about it.

04:38.487 --> 04:40.822
There were a lot of papers on that topic.

04:41.531 --> 04:45.619
If you're reading academic papers,
this isn't just a casual interest.

04:45.702 --> 04:49.331
But how can you know my whole background
and still not recognize my face?

04:49.873 --> 04:53.543
I just never imagined
you'd be here running a farm.

04:53.627 --> 04:55.670
[chuckles softly]
Then what did you imagine?

04:55.754 --> 04:59.299
[inhales deeply]
What was the most popular theory? Russia?

04:59.382 --> 05:01.009
That you were tied to the Russian Mafia.

05:01.092 --> 05:02.135
[chuckles]

05:02.219 --> 05:05.806
That you had gambling debts in Macau,
or even that you embezzled 50 billion won.

05:05.889 --> 05:09.476
But I never believed any of it.
It all sounded like nonsense.

05:09.559 --> 05:10.602
Impressive.

05:10.685 --> 05:13.104
But you skipped the
"betrayed by a business partner" rumor.

05:13.188 --> 05:14.564
Did you believe that one?

05:16.191 --> 05:19.361
[chuckles softly] It's all just gossip.

05:19.444 --> 05:21.238
Mr. Lee, the CEO, wasn't that bad.

05:21.863 --> 05:23.073
Then again,

05:23.156 --> 05:26.117
he wasn't exactly the type
to brave a typhoon for a partner.

05:26.993 --> 05:27.994
Jeez.

05:30.163 --> 05:34.000
Seriously though, why did you quit?

05:34.084 --> 05:36.169
You disappeared overnight.

05:37.754 --> 05:38.964
Do you want to know?

05:42.551 --> 05:44.469
I'll tell you the day after tomorrow.

05:45.262 --> 05:49.307
Gosh, why the day after tomorrow
and not tomorrow?

05:49.391 --> 05:51.434
That just seems like the right time.

05:52.394 --> 05:53.728
[inhales deeply]

05:53.812 --> 05:56.398
But now that we're talking,
I've got a question too.

05:58.441 --> 06:00.360
What are you doing here?

06:01.194 --> 06:04.322
For someone this quiet
to go on and on like that,

06:04.406 --> 06:06.658
you must clearly love this stuff.

06:07.200 --> 06:09.286
Ever considered working in finance?

06:09.786 --> 06:10.912
- I…
- [Se-jin] For now,

06:10.996 --> 06:14.082
forget about your educational background
or qualifications.

06:14.165 --> 06:15.750
I want to know how you really feel.

06:16.751 --> 06:17.752
Well,

06:18.420 --> 06:21.506
just because you like something
doesn't mean you can do it.

06:23.008 --> 06:24.217
Why not?

06:24.301 --> 06:26.261
Every family has its own issues,

06:26.344 --> 06:29.347
and mine is no different.
I can't just think about myself.

06:29.973 --> 06:31.558
- Why not?
- [Mi-rae] What do you mean?

06:31.641 --> 06:33.685
My family has sacrificed so much for me.

06:34.728 --> 06:36.313
How could I just do whatever I want?

06:36.396 --> 06:38.106
[inhales deeply]

06:39.816 --> 06:41.693
Honestly, everything you're saying

06:41.776 --> 06:43.737
is no different
from the Russian Mafia rumors.

06:45.280 --> 06:46.281
What?

06:46.907 --> 06:48.199
Those are not the real reasons.

06:49.910 --> 06:51.661
I want to know the real one.

06:52.871 --> 06:55.081
[gentle music playing]

06:56.439 --> 07:01.087
EPISODE 7
A CHILD UNDERNEATH IT ALL

07:01.171 --> 07:02.923
[gentle music continues]

07:03.465 --> 07:05.258
[elevator dings]

07:06.392 --> 07:10.817
KOREA FINANCE MANAGEMENT CORPORATION

07:10.931 --> 07:12.265
[cell phone buzzes]

07:15.310 --> 07:18.396
[Mi-ji] You're on your way, right?
It's the same meeting room as before.

07:18.480 --> 07:19.731
YU MI-RAE

07:19.814 --> 07:21.274
[Ho-su] I'm almost there.

07:22.734 --> 07:24.736
[Ho-su]
You want me to decline, no matter what?

07:24.819 --> 07:27.155
Next time you go to the office,

07:27.238 --> 07:30.659
just tell them I'm not selling.

07:30.742 --> 07:34.454
But we gained the upper hand
in the last meeting.

07:34.537 --> 07:38.166
I can negotiate any terms you want.

07:38.249 --> 07:40.877
I don't want anything.

07:40.961 --> 07:45.548
Just wrap it up neatly
so nothing else comes up.

07:46.424 --> 07:48.593
And so your friend gets in less trouble.

07:50.095 --> 07:51.221
[knocking on door]

07:51.304 --> 07:52.514
[Mi-ji] Come on in.

07:54.557 --> 07:56.351
He's here. [chuckles]

07:59.771 --> 08:02.983
[soft tense music playing]

08:06.152 --> 08:08.613
I was wondering
which law firm you ended up at.

08:10.073 --> 08:13.368
If I'd known you opened your own,
I would've at least sent flowers.

08:13.451 --> 08:15.078
Let's just say you did.

08:16.371 --> 08:19.791
You came all this way to see me
for such a minor case.

08:21.584 --> 08:24.337
It's funny how people cross paths.

08:25.005 --> 08:29.300
Just like unpaid bills,
some people are impossible to avoid.

08:30.301 --> 08:33.388
I heard you were one
of Kim Ro-sa's scholarship students.

08:33.471 --> 08:36.224
Did you take this case to repay her?

08:37.600 --> 08:38.601
Or…

08:39.102 --> 08:41.521
is it out of guilt for an old classmate?

08:41.604 --> 08:42.981
WHISTLEBLOWER INVESTIGATION REPORT

08:43.940 --> 08:45.358
[sighs]

08:45.442 --> 08:47.819
She already knows everything.

08:47.902 --> 08:50.697
But she doesn't know
you're the one who made me

08:50.780 --> 08:52.407
the external investigator for the case.

08:53.491 --> 08:55.577
Ms. Yu Mi-rae must be important to you

08:55.660 --> 08:57.579
if you told her all that.

08:57.662 --> 08:58.872
Let us get to the point.

08:58.955 --> 09:00.248
[music fades]

09:00.749 --> 09:04.586
My client is not interested
in selling the Rosa Restaurant.

09:05.295 --> 09:08.006
I'm here today
to officially decline the offer.

09:09.090 --> 09:12.469
You're turning it down flat,
without even negotiating. Why?

09:12.552 --> 09:15.013
The landowner does not want to sell.

09:15.555 --> 09:17.390
Do you need any other reason?

09:20.101 --> 09:22.479
[soft tense music playing]

09:24.689 --> 09:26.024
So you don't know either.

09:27.275 --> 09:28.234
Excuse me?

09:28.318 --> 09:30.987
There's always a reason
behind an unreasonable choice.

09:31.071 --> 09:34.032
If you do not know what it is,

09:34.657 --> 09:36.743
it means you either didn't care to ask,

09:36.826 --> 09:40.455
or you're not trusted enough to be told.

09:41.664 --> 09:43.041
It's one or the other.

09:47.128 --> 09:48.129
Ho-su.

09:49.506 --> 09:50.507
That's your problem.

09:51.800 --> 09:54.719
You never cross the line,
all for your stubborn integrity.

09:54.803 --> 09:56.679
You know what's going on
but remain silent.

09:56.763 --> 09:59.140
That's not being considerate.

09:59.224 --> 10:00.642
That's neglect.

10:01.434 --> 10:04.437
You came here
just to say she's not selling?

10:04.521 --> 10:08.817
That doesn't help Ms. Kim Ro-sa
or Ms. Yu one bit.

10:09.818 --> 10:13.029
If anything, I'm the one helping them.

10:13.113 --> 10:15.323
You are not helping. You are using them.

10:16.116 --> 10:17.200
For your own benefit.

10:18.576 --> 10:22.872
Do you even know
what Mi-rae's going through at work?

10:24.707 --> 10:26.042
I do.

10:26.126 --> 10:29.045
And I am trying to fix it.

10:29.129 --> 10:30.672
Call it whatever you want,

10:30.755 --> 10:33.758
but I am trying
to tip the scales in her favor.

10:34.342 --> 10:35.927
You are the one

10:37.011 --> 10:38.596
ruining that right now.

10:38.680 --> 10:40.974
- Sir.
- [Chung-gu] So I'm telling you

10:41.057 --> 10:42.350
to cross the line.

10:43.226 --> 10:44.602
Don't just stand by.

10:45.228 --> 10:47.063
Ask why and persuade her.

10:47.147 --> 10:48.773
I'm giving you a chance.

10:49.399 --> 10:51.985
Use it to help the people
who are important to you.

10:52.861 --> 10:53.862
A chance?

10:53.945 --> 10:55.572
She'll sell in the end.

10:56.489 --> 10:57.615
You know me.

10:59.159 --> 11:02.078
If I want something, I get it.

11:04.914 --> 11:06.499
- [music fades]
- [door opens]

11:10.670 --> 11:12.714
Hey, are you done already?

11:13.339 --> 11:15.633
[Chung-gu]
Figure out how you can help everyone.

11:15.717 --> 11:16.968
Think hard.

11:19.512 --> 11:20.555
[sighs]

11:24.684 --> 11:27.437
[Mi-ji] Did he always look like this?

11:28.062 --> 11:30.190
His lashes are pretty long.

11:31.357 --> 11:33.234
Did he shape his brows?

11:34.485 --> 11:37.322
And it looks like
he put something on his lips.

11:38.823 --> 11:40.533
[quirky music playing]

11:40.617 --> 11:42.368
- What?
- Nothing.

11:43.536 --> 11:44.454
[inhales]

11:44.537 --> 11:45.622
Hey.

11:46.122 --> 11:48.082
Are you busy next week?

11:48.708 --> 11:49.876
Next week?

11:51.127 --> 11:52.212
Uh…

11:52.295 --> 11:53.296
Why?

11:54.339 --> 11:56.507
I was thinking
of getting you and Mi-ji together.

11:56.591 --> 11:57.592
[coughs]

11:59.302 --> 12:00.637
[Ho-su] What?

12:00.720 --> 12:02.263
It's just that…

12:02.347 --> 12:05.266
she said she'd be in Seoul
sometime next week.

12:05.350 --> 12:08.645
You said she's your first love.
You two should really talk.

12:09.270 --> 12:11.022
She didn't go into details,

12:11.105 --> 12:13.816
but apparently,
she has something to say to you.

12:15.360 --> 12:17.195
Oh, well…

12:17.278 --> 12:19.822
Then just pick a time that works for her.

12:19.906 --> 12:21.282
[chuckles]

12:21.366 --> 12:22.450
Cool.

12:23.201 --> 12:26.913
[sighs] Seriously,
what would you two do without me?

12:30.458 --> 12:32.001
[music concludes]

12:36.756 --> 12:37.715
[Ho-su] Hey…

12:38.633 --> 12:40.385
You don't have to walk me out.

12:42.011 --> 12:43.471
I'm going out for lunch.

12:44.264 --> 12:45.932
Do you want to join me?

12:48.059 --> 12:50.228
I have to meet someone today.

12:50.937 --> 12:52.188
Oh.

12:52.272 --> 12:53.815
All right. Go ahead then.

12:57.485 --> 12:58.945
[sighs]

12:59.028 --> 13:00.113
Hey…

13:01.239 --> 13:02.282
Let me know

13:03.241 --> 13:04.450
when you

13:04.993 --> 13:06.202
set something up with Mi-ji.

13:07.954 --> 13:09.080
Sure.

13:10.581 --> 13:11.749
See you.

13:19.340 --> 13:20.842
[cell phone buzzes]

13:28.474 --> 13:31.602
[Ji-yun] Let's talk.
We have things to discuss.

13:31.686 --> 13:34.272
What does she need to talk about?

13:35.231 --> 13:36.566
Is it about Ho-su?

13:49.370 --> 13:50.705
Why are you still here?

13:53.583 --> 13:56.836
I'm just waiting for someone.

13:57.920 --> 13:59.797
Is this seat taken?

13:59.881 --> 14:01.174
[chuckles softly]

14:03.092 --> 14:04.594
Now you're mocking me.

14:04.677 --> 14:05.887
[dark intriguing music playing]

14:05.970 --> 14:06.971
[woman] Right.

14:07.055 --> 14:10.850
I guess you'd have to be that shameless
to keep showing up at work.

14:10.933 --> 14:12.268
[Mi-ji sighs]

14:12.352 --> 14:14.604
Excuse me. Who are you to--

14:14.687 --> 14:16.356
That's disappointing.

14:16.439 --> 14:19.192
I haven't gone a day
without thinking about you, Ms. Yu.

14:21.694 --> 14:22.779
It's me.

14:24.072 --> 14:25.531
Park Sang-yeong's wife.

14:30.286 --> 14:31.621
Now you remember?

14:32.413 --> 14:35.166
Don't you remember
what I told you, though?

14:35.666 --> 14:37.085
If you had any decency,

14:37.168 --> 14:39.587
you should've disappeared
before he came back.

14:39.670 --> 14:42.256
Wasn't everything
humiliating enough for you?

14:42.340 --> 14:44.467
[exhales] What are you talking about--

14:44.550 --> 14:45.593
[Ji-yun] Excuse me.

14:46.594 --> 14:49.222
What the heck are you doing?
She's my friend.

14:49.305 --> 14:51.015
Stay out of this.

14:51.682 --> 14:54.644
This is between me and Ms. Yu Mi-rae.

14:55.520 --> 14:57.647
- [music builds]
- Then go talk to Yu Mi-rae.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.982
Why the hell are you taking it out
on the wrong person?

15:00.066 --> 15:01.734
[music fades]

15:01.818 --> 15:02.902
What?

15:03.903 --> 15:07.073
She isn't Yu Mi-rae.

15:08.074 --> 15:11.577
What… are you talking about…

15:11.661 --> 15:15.039
If you've got the wrong person,
shouldn't you apologize first?

15:15.123 --> 15:17.041
You're a new level of crazy.

15:17.125 --> 15:19.293
Mi-ji, let's go.

15:20.169 --> 15:21.212
What?

15:26.676 --> 15:29.011
Why did you just sit there and take it?

15:29.095 --> 15:30.721
Are you copying Mi-rae even on that?

15:32.849 --> 15:34.642
Ji-yun, how did you…

15:34.725 --> 15:37.270
Gosh, how do you think?

15:37.353 --> 15:40.148
You always froze up
whenever I mentioned KFMC.

15:40.231 --> 15:41.983
So I tested you.

15:42.066 --> 15:45.653
Would you have applied there
if I hadn't pushed you to?

15:45.736 --> 15:47.155
Honestly?

15:47.238 --> 15:48.322
You're right.

15:50.450 --> 15:54.287
Why would I encourage Mi-rae to apply
to the place I was dying to get into?

15:54.370 --> 15:56.998
And she's not the kind to do something
just because I told her to.

15:57.081 --> 15:58.332
[sighs]

15:58.416 --> 16:00.585
That's what gave it away?

16:00.668 --> 16:04.338
What really confirmed it

16:05.047 --> 16:07.091
was what you said after.

16:08.009 --> 16:09.051
What did I say?

16:09.135 --> 16:10.970
That I sounded very mature

16:11.053 --> 16:13.014
and you liked how honest I was.

16:13.556 --> 16:15.683
That's the kind of thing you'd say, Mi-ji.

16:16.392 --> 16:18.227
That's when I knew it was you.

16:21.814 --> 16:22.899
At least,

16:23.774 --> 16:25.568
I got to see you again.

16:27.069 --> 16:28.946
I always wondered how you were doing.

16:29.989 --> 16:32.825
But I didn't reach out
since you didn't like me.

16:33.367 --> 16:35.661
Why would I not like you?

16:35.745 --> 16:37.288
Don't play dumb.

16:37.371 --> 16:39.499
You totally avoided me back then.

16:40.541 --> 16:41.792
I just thought

16:42.585 --> 16:44.754
you were disappointed in me.

16:45.463 --> 16:46.839
Hey.

16:46.923 --> 16:48.591
I am your number one fan.

16:49.509 --> 16:51.260
Why would I ever be disappointed?

16:52.428 --> 16:55.014
That doesn't even make sense.

16:55.097 --> 16:57.767
- [calm chatter]
- [mellow pop music playing over speakers]

16:58.309 --> 16:59.477
[inhales deeply]

17:00.019 --> 17:03.105
So what was it
you wanted to talk about today?

17:03.898 --> 17:04.941
Forget it.

17:05.525 --> 17:09.445
I was pissed you stole Ho-su,
so I thought I'd make a scene.

17:10.071 --> 17:13.658
But then I ended up arguing
with some random person instead.

17:14.659 --> 17:16.786
Have you told Ho-su?

17:17.411 --> 17:18.538
Does he know?

17:19.622 --> 17:20.790
I don't know.

17:21.374 --> 17:22.542
Maybe he does.

17:23.125 --> 17:24.794
Maybe he doesn't.

17:24.877 --> 17:27.338
So does he or doesn't he?

17:27.421 --> 17:29.549
I'm not helping you with that.

17:29.632 --> 17:31.300
Ask him yourself.

17:33.261 --> 17:36.806
But seriously,
why didn't you say anything earlier?

17:36.889 --> 17:40.977
I thought you'd at least
grab her hair or something.

17:41.060 --> 17:42.478
You know her?

17:42.979 --> 17:44.897
Do you know anything about her?

17:45.690 --> 17:47.108
You really don't know?

17:49.860 --> 17:51.904
Mi-rae didn't tell you about the rumors?

17:53.823 --> 17:55.283
- What rumors?
- [pensive music playing]

17:55.366 --> 17:59.537
[Ji-yun] There were rumors about
Mi-rae having an affair with her boss.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.455
PS TEAM HOMEWRECKER GOT DRAGGED

18:01.539 --> 18:03.082
That woman was his wife.

18:03.874 --> 18:06.794
She threw a fit at Mi-rae
in the company lobby,

18:06.877 --> 18:07.920
so the rumors spread.

18:08.004 --> 18:10.923
Hey, don't you know her?

18:11.007 --> 18:13.634
She's a total stickler
when it comes to stuff like that.

18:13.718 --> 18:16.721
An affair? With a married man?

18:16.804 --> 18:19.640
Are you crazy?
She has no reason to stoop to that.

18:19.724 --> 18:21.934
I didn't believe it at first, either.

18:22.435 --> 18:24.687
But then people from KFMC
started commenting online,

18:24.770 --> 18:27.189
and photos of her were spreading around.

18:27.273 --> 18:28.274
I mean…

18:29.150 --> 18:30.776
no one knows the full story.

18:30.860 --> 18:32.361
She would never.

18:32.445 --> 18:34.113
I can't believe you bought that.

18:34.196 --> 18:38.117
Regardless of whether it's true or not,
it was a huge deal.

18:38.200 --> 18:41.370
I saw the rumors
on the KFMC job prep forums.

18:41.912 --> 18:43.789
Imagine what it was like at her office.

18:43.873 --> 18:47.668
I'll send you the link. See for yourself.

18:47.752 --> 18:50.212
[sighs] Mi-rae, seriously…

18:50.838 --> 18:53.090
Why didn't you tell me about any of this?

18:53.966 --> 18:55.718
[Ok-hui sighs]

18:55.801 --> 18:57.428
- [music fades]
- [door closes]

18:57.928 --> 18:59.055
Were you home?

18:59.555 --> 19:01.390
When did you get back? I didn't hear you.

19:01.474 --> 19:03.184
I got back at the crack of dawn.

19:03.267 --> 19:05.728
But why are you leaving for work now?

19:06.270 --> 19:09.190
The school's temporarily closed.
They're doing typhoon recovery work.

19:09.273 --> 19:11.859
It was chaos while you were in Seoul.

19:11.942 --> 19:13.778
Power went out, bridges flooded…

19:13.861 --> 19:15.738
Oh. Really?

19:16.697 --> 19:19.492
Good thing Gyeong-gu got you to Seoul
before things got crazy.

19:19.575 --> 19:21.827
It's been a while
since you went that far. Rest up.

19:21.911 --> 19:23.913
- I'm heading out.
- Okay. Bye, Mom.

19:23.996 --> 19:25.539
[Ok-hui] Okay, go get some rest.

19:25.623 --> 19:27.416
All right. [exhales]

19:27.500 --> 19:29.085
[sliding door opens, closes]

19:30.836 --> 19:32.004
[Ok-hui] Mi-ji.

19:32.546 --> 19:33.673
Mi-ji!

19:33.756 --> 19:35.049
What?

19:35.132 --> 19:37.927
[Ok-hui] Here she comes. Come quickly!

19:40.471 --> 19:42.056
Ho-su wants to talk to you.

19:42.139 --> 19:44.975
I'm leaving. You two have a chat.

19:45.059 --> 19:46.477
See you, Ho-su.

19:48.354 --> 19:50.523
Do you want something to drink?

19:51.565 --> 19:52.608
Sure.

19:56.570 --> 20:00.324
What did you need to talk about
that made you come all this way?

20:00.908 --> 20:02.159
We never got to

20:03.077 --> 20:04.203
talk properly.

20:06.664 --> 20:09.333
Didn't you say
everything you wanted to last time?

20:09.417 --> 20:11.335
- [drink pouring]
- Not to you.

20:12.378 --> 20:13.713
- Mi-rae.
- [pouring stops]

20:13.796 --> 20:16.590
[soft pensive music playing]

20:22.805 --> 20:24.140
[music fades]

20:24.223 --> 20:25.850
[Ok-hui] Oh my. Hello.

20:26.350 --> 20:27.685
Oh dear.

20:27.768 --> 20:30.062
- What a disaster.
- [woman] It's a total mess.

20:30.146 --> 20:32.565
The school's a wreck.

20:33.232 --> 20:34.692
Hey, should I join you?

20:34.775 --> 20:37.653
Actually, could you head up
to the second floor?

20:37.737 --> 20:39.572
We need to mop up there.

20:40.448 --> 20:41.574
Sure thing.

20:44.285 --> 20:46.203
- By the way…
- [Bun-hong] What?

20:47.037 --> 20:48.456
Your son's here.

20:49.206 --> 20:50.166
Ho-su?

20:50.666 --> 20:51.959
He didn't say he was coming.

20:52.918 --> 20:54.128
Are you sure?

20:54.211 --> 20:56.380
He came to my house.

20:56.464 --> 20:58.632
He had something to discuss with Mi-ji.

21:00.176 --> 21:02.511
What would my Ho-su
need to discuss with Mi-ji?

21:03.888 --> 21:06.766
How should I know?
He's the one who came by.

21:06.849 --> 21:09.518
Whatever it was, he looked so serious

21:09.602 --> 21:11.187
that it made Mi-ji flustered.

21:11.771 --> 21:13.564
Maybe there's something
going on between them

21:13.647 --> 21:14.815
and you just don't know.

21:14.899 --> 21:17.777
You might end up as in-laws.

21:17.860 --> 21:19.779
- [laughs]
- Come on, in-laws?

21:19.862 --> 21:21.447
[Bun-hong] They're not like that.

21:22.072 --> 21:23.574
What a thing to say.

21:24.658 --> 21:27.203
Why so serious over a joke?

21:27.286 --> 21:28.913
You're making things awkward.

21:29.747 --> 21:31.290
Come on.

21:31.373 --> 21:34.001
Ho-su and Mi-ji are barely acquaintances.

21:34.084 --> 21:35.211
What she said was nonsense.

21:35.294 --> 21:36.879
Jeez.

21:36.962 --> 21:39.965
Are you suggesting
that my daughter isn't good enough?

21:40.549 --> 21:41.926
Hey.

21:42.009 --> 21:45.262
I don't want a son-in-law
who has to be waited on hand and foot.

21:58.234 --> 22:00.820
- [sighs]
- What was that supposed to mean?

22:00.903 --> 22:02.154
You startled me.

22:02.238 --> 22:04.114
What are you talking about?

22:04.198 --> 22:06.826
"A son-in-law who has to be
waited on hand and foot."

22:06.909 --> 22:08.661
What about it?

22:08.744 --> 22:11.455
- It means your son is successful.
- You didn't mean that.

22:11.539 --> 22:14.291
You were clearly referring
to his physical issues.

22:14.375 --> 22:17.086
Goodness, what the heck?

22:17.169 --> 22:18.504
Don't you get metaphors?

22:18.587 --> 22:21.131
[shouting] Why use that kind of metaphor?

22:21.215 --> 22:23.217
- Do you think he's an invalid?
- [tense music playing]

22:23.300 --> 22:24.635
- Or a patient?
- What's with you?

22:24.718 --> 22:25.886
- He can't move?
- Bun-hong.

22:25.970 --> 22:28.138
- Why would anyone need to wait on him?
- For God's sake!

22:28.222 --> 22:30.015
Did you just push me?

22:30.766 --> 22:31.934
Apologize.

22:32.017 --> 22:33.561
For what you said.

22:33.644 --> 22:35.020
Goodness me.

22:35.104 --> 22:37.231
I've got nothing to apologize for!

22:37.314 --> 22:39.984
I didn't mean that.
Why are you making such a fuss?

22:40.067 --> 22:42.361
Seriously. Move!

22:43.153 --> 22:45.197
Do you have
a victim mentality or something?

22:45.281 --> 22:47.741
Give me a break. Jeez.

22:49.952 --> 22:51.579
[screams]

22:51.662 --> 22:53.330
[music fades]

22:55.624 --> 22:56.917
Can we talk now?

22:58.252 --> 22:59.545
Did Mi-ji tell you?

23:00.421 --> 23:02.214
Are you two still meeting up?

23:03.299 --> 23:05.426
If you're asking how I knew it was you,

23:06.051 --> 23:08.178
I figured it out
after I saw you last time.

23:09.263 --> 23:11.307
So you kept meeting up after all,

23:11.390 --> 23:13.475
seeing how you didn't answer my question.

23:14.184 --> 23:15.185
Does that…

23:16.145 --> 23:17.146
matter to you?

23:17.938 --> 23:19.189
Of course it does.

23:19.773 --> 23:22.026
I told her to stop meeting you,

23:22.109 --> 23:24.028
and Mi-ji promised she would.

23:25.988 --> 23:27.197
So,

23:28.365 --> 23:30.200
what did you want to talk about?

23:31.452 --> 23:32.953
About Lead Specialist Park.

23:33.621 --> 23:37.249
You filed a sexual harassment report
and then suddenly withdrew it.

23:37.333 --> 23:38.626
Why?

23:38.709 --> 23:40.461
That's over. What business is it of yours?

23:40.544 --> 23:43.005
That's what I'm asking.
Did you do that because of me?

23:43.088 --> 23:44.590
[pensive music playing]

23:44.673 --> 23:47.051
The day I came in
as an external investigator,

23:47.134 --> 23:50.679
you disappeared as soon as you saw me,
and then you dropped the case.

23:51.221 --> 23:53.891
I figured it was because of me,
but you ignored all my calls.

23:53.974 --> 23:56.435
Now your twin is coming in
to work instead of you.

23:58.187 --> 23:59.396
Is it really over?

24:00.022 --> 24:02.900
Did you tell Mi-ji about this?

24:04.276 --> 24:06.362
I thought she was you,
so I mentioned the case.

24:07.905 --> 24:10.658
But Mi-ji seemed clueless,
and I didn't know much either.

24:10.741 --> 24:11.700
So,

24:12.368 --> 24:14.078
I came to ask you directly.

24:14.870 --> 24:16.121
To see if I could help.

24:18.749 --> 24:19.959
Help?

24:22.127 --> 24:24.171
Who asked for your help?

24:24.254 --> 24:26.131
It got complicated because of me.

24:27.633 --> 24:28.801
Let me fix it.

24:34.056 --> 24:37.434
What exactly happened
between you and Park Sang-yeong?

24:41.271 --> 24:43.023
You're crossing a line.

24:45.526 --> 24:46.819
I came to cross it.

24:52.241 --> 24:54.201
[cell phone buzzing]

24:57.121 --> 24:58.455
MOM

24:58.539 --> 25:01.291
[cell phones buzzing]

25:01.915 --> 25:03.669
MOM

25:03.752 --> 25:05.421
[music fades]

25:06.380 --> 25:07.881
SORRY I MADE YOU
GO THROUGH THIS ALONE

25:07.965 --> 25:10.968
[Tae-i] You accepted this project
knowing Mr. Park is in charge?

25:11.051 --> 25:13.429
[Mi-ji] I made Mi-rae
look like a total psycho.

25:13.512 --> 25:15.973
[sighs]
But why didn't she tell me anything?

25:16.056 --> 25:19.059
She said she was standing up
for a senior who blew the whistle.

25:19.143 --> 25:20.894
Then those jerks bullied you for a year

25:20.978 --> 25:23.605
just because you said that
during the interview?

25:23.689 --> 25:25.065
[intriguing music playing]

25:25.566 --> 25:28.360
People don't need
a lot of reasons to hate someone.

25:28.444 --> 25:29.653
[Ho-su] Did you drop the case…

25:29.737 --> 25:31.530
WHISTLEBLOWER INVESTIGATION REPORT

25:31.613 --> 25:34.074
In cases like this,
when it's about sexual misconduct,

25:34.158 --> 25:37.411
sometimes the victim drops the case

25:37.494 --> 25:39.872
because they're worried
about rumors spreading.

25:44.207 --> 25:45.794
PS TEAM HOMEWRECKER GOT DRAGGED

25:45.878 --> 25:48.464
[Mi-rae] If I tell you not to look,
just don't look.

25:49.006 --> 25:51.759
We promised
not to interfere in each other's lives.

25:51.842 --> 25:52.885
[sighs]

25:54.261 --> 25:56.055
I'll hear it from her later.

25:57.931 --> 25:59.391
MI-JI

25:59.475 --> 26:01.435
[music fades]

26:01.518 --> 26:03.145
- [Mi-ji] Hmm?
- [cell phone buzzing]

26:03.771 --> 26:04.646
[Ok-hui muttering]

26:04.730 --> 26:06.857
- Ms. Kim Ok-hui and Yeom Bun-hong.
- That's us.

26:06.940 --> 26:08.317
You both slipped on the stairs…

26:08.400 --> 26:10.736
- It was her. She pushed me.
- …and showed signs of concussion.

26:10.819 --> 26:13.072
- She yanked my hair.
- [doctor] The stitches were done well.

26:13.155 --> 26:16.825
The orthopedist will decide tomorrow
whether you need metal pins.

26:16.909 --> 26:19.411
A semi-private room just opened up,

26:19.495 --> 26:22.081
so we'll keep them for one night or two
and see how it goes.

26:22.164 --> 26:25.167
Mi-ji, I can't share a room with her.

26:25.250 --> 26:27.377
- No way.
- Mom, what happened?

26:27.461 --> 26:29.463
How did you both fall down the stairs?

26:29.546 --> 26:31.381
You know what? I shouldn't be here.

26:31.465 --> 26:32.966
I should be at the police station.

26:33.050 --> 26:35.302
Who grabs someone by the hair
on the stairs?

26:35.385 --> 26:37.221
That's attempted murder!

26:37.304 --> 26:38.514
- Jeez.
- Good God.

26:38.597 --> 26:41.350
- [quirky music playing]
- You're making a fuss over a few stitches?

26:41.433 --> 26:43.811
- I might get a pin put in here.
- [Ok-hui chuckles] Whatever.

26:43.894 --> 26:46.980
You can't blame me for your own fall.

26:47.064 --> 26:48.524
It was self-defense for me!

26:48.607 --> 26:51.860
I see. Should we sort it out legally?

26:51.944 --> 26:52.903
"Sort it out legally"?

26:52.986 --> 26:54.196
- Ho-su.
- [Ok-hui] Good. Tell us.

26:54.279 --> 26:57.407
Let's ask your lawyer son
what the law says and settle this.

26:57.491 --> 26:59.743
Please. Calm down, both of you.

26:59.827 --> 27:01.286
Check the surveillance footage.

27:01.370 --> 27:03.705
Your mom pushed me. You know how she is.

27:03.789 --> 27:06.083
- What?
- [Ok-hui] What did you say?

27:06.166 --> 27:08.961
You'll be punished for this, Bun-hong.

27:09.044 --> 27:10.504
- Mom, stop.
- You little…

27:10.587 --> 27:12.339
- I'm gonna win. You just watch.
- [Mi-rae] Mom.

27:12.422 --> 27:15.134
- [Ok-hui] Look at all the hair…
- Close the curtain. She's embarrassing.

27:15.217 --> 27:16.093
…you pulled out!

27:16.176 --> 27:19.596
Look, there's still hair
coming out of my head!

27:19.680 --> 27:21.140
[music concludes]

27:22.808 --> 27:24.017
Jeez.

27:28.730 --> 27:30.065
Did you call Mi-ji here?

27:31.567 --> 27:32.693
Yes. Why?

27:32.776 --> 27:34.570
Mi-ji doesn't know that I know.

27:34.653 --> 27:37.030
- So?
- I know it's a weird thing to ask,

27:37.114 --> 27:39.116
but can we pretend
that I don't know anything?

27:39.199 --> 27:40.826
- Please?
- Hey.

27:40.909 --> 27:42.161
Mi-rae!

27:43.787 --> 27:46.540
[soft quirky music playing]

27:53.380 --> 27:55.757
- [music fades]
- Why did you ask me to come all of sudden?

27:55.841 --> 27:57.176
And why are we in the hospital?

27:57.259 --> 28:00.179
Mom got into a fight with Bun-hong
and got a little hurt.

28:00.262 --> 28:01.972
She'll have to stay for a day or two.

28:02.055 --> 28:05.684
What? Is that why Ho-su came down too?

28:06.476 --> 28:08.103
She's asking why you're here.

28:08.937 --> 28:12.399
I… just had something to take care of.

28:12.482 --> 28:13.483
I see.

28:14.109 --> 28:16.361
You had something to take care of.

28:19.156 --> 28:20.032
[Mi-rae sighs]

28:22.492 --> 28:23.535
[horn honks]

28:24.870 --> 28:26.121
[sighs]

28:26.997 --> 28:28.290
How did you…

28:28.373 --> 28:30.000
I told you I'd be late today.

28:30.083 --> 28:31.543
I heard your mother was hospitalized.

28:31.627 --> 28:34.421
I always get concerned
about the health issues of elders.

28:34.504 --> 28:37.007
[Mi-rae] Mom's fine, so you can…

28:37.090 --> 28:38.467
What the…

28:38.550 --> 28:40.344
[soft quirky music playing]

28:40.969 --> 28:42.054
Ms. Seoul?

28:42.763 --> 28:44.139
You look exactly…

28:44.932 --> 28:46.558
She looks exactly like you!

28:46.642 --> 28:47.726
Who are you?

28:47.809 --> 28:49.853
It's me, the strawberry farmer!

28:49.937 --> 28:51.897
Wait. You didn't send the strawberries?

28:52.564 --> 28:54.816
Ah! That 200,000-won gig?

28:55.776 --> 28:58.028
So you've told her about me.

28:59.404 --> 29:02.199
We've met before, right?
You were waiting outside the house.

29:02.282 --> 29:03.575
Oh, yes.

29:03.659 --> 29:04.910
Hello.

29:06.328 --> 29:07.746
You should go now.

29:07.829 --> 29:10.040
Go where? I've got nowhere to be.

29:10.666 --> 29:12.417
No one's eaten yet, right?

29:12.501 --> 29:15.212
Since we've run into each other,
let's go eat together.

29:19.591 --> 29:21.843
Why are you three exchanging glances?

29:21.927 --> 29:24.388
I see. You're trying to leave me out.

29:24.930 --> 29:27.349
- Everyone's tired, so--
- Come on.

29:27.432 --> 29:29.434
You still need to eat.

29:29.518 --> 29:31.520
I'll treat you to something really good.

29:33.105 --> 29:34.773
No more exchanging glances!

29:34.856 --> 29:37.317
- [music concludes]
- You all eat intestines, right?

29:37.901 --> 29:38.944
Excuse me.

29:39.027 --> 29:40.279
- Hi.
- [Se-jin] Hello.

29:40.904 --> 29:43.740
Intestines hot pot for three
and one pork cutlet, please.

29:43.824 --> 29:44.908
[waitress] Sure.

29:46.034 --> 29:49.371
I can't handle the intestines.
I've got a weak stomach.

29:49.454 --> 29:51.957
But this place is famous. [gulps]

29:52.916 --> 29:55.460
[Se-jin] Ah. [exhales]

29:56.044 --> 29:57.087
[inhales deeply]

29:57.170 --> 29:59.423
Should I take the lead here?

30:01.049 --> 30:04.052
Let's introduce ourselves first.
We'll go around in a circle.

30:05.429 --> 30:07.139
I'm Han Se-jin. Next!

30:10.517 --> 30:11.727
I'm Lee Ho-su.

30:13.687 --> 30:14.771
Uh…

30:15.814 --> 30:18.275
- I'm Yu Mi-rae.
- [Se-jin] Mi-rae?

30:18.358 --> 30:20.402
I like that name.

30:20.485 --> 30:22.904
[inhales deeply]
I heard you've been living in Seoul.

30:22.988 --> 30:26.158
Where do you work--
Is that too personal?

30:26.241 --> 30:29.369
I work at KFMC.
Korea Finance Management Corporation.

30:29.453 --> 30:31.330
[Se-jin] Oh, impressive.

30:31.413 --> 30:35.042
Did you major in that field--
Is that too personal?

30:36.168 --> 30:37.336
Well…

30:38.337 --> 30:40.047
I majored in economics.

30:41.006 --> 30:42.674
You should ask her then.

30:42.758 --> 30:44.551
My business partner here
is passionate about it

30:44.634 --> 30:46.428
and digs through academic papers.

30:46.511 --> 30:50.140
[inhales deeply] Do sisters
always have such similar interests?

30:50.223 --> 30:52.184
- Fascinating.
- Wow.

30:52.267 --> 30:55.062
- [soft quirky music playing]
- I didn't know that about her.

30:55.729 --> 30:57.898
What about you, Ho-su?

30:57.981 --> 31:00.108
Wait. Don't say it. Let me guess.

31:00.192 --> 31:02.402
I'm really good at this, so watch out.

31:02.986 --> 31:04.112
[inhales]

31:04.696 --> 31:05.947
Law?

31:06.031 --> 31:07.366
I smell law.

31:08.450 --> 31:10.035
You're in law school!

31:12.579 --> 31:15.207
- I graduated.
- Wait, what? Oh my God.

31:15.290 --> 31:17.626
- [music concludes]
- I got it right! Look at these goosebumps.

31:17.709 --> 31:19.169
[inhales deeply, exhales]

31:19.252 --> 31:20.337
By the way,

31:21.004 --> 31:23.215
where's your farm located?

31:23.298 --> 31:25.217
I might know it.

31:25.967 --> 31:28.303
You've been living in Seoul,
so you probably don't.

31:28.387 --> 31:30.597
It's across the bridge.
It's called Changhwa Farm.

31:30.680 --> 31:31.848
[Mi-ji] What?

31:31.932 --> 31:34.518
Isn't that the place
an old gentleman used to run by himself?

31:34.601 --> 31:36.353
His grandson studied abroad.

31:36.436 --> 31:37.896
Did you know my grandfather?

31:38.438 --> 31:41.066
Yes. He was super quiet.

31:41.858 --> 31:46.154
[chuckles] The only time he spoke
was when he bragged about his grandson.

31:47.322 --> 31:48.824
So you're that grandson.

31:49.449 --> 31:50.992
My goodness…

31:51.576 --> 31:53.495
Hearing about my grandfather
from someone else

31:53.578 --> 31:54.746
is making me emotional.

31:54.830 --> 31:58.875
He called you a kid,
so I thought you were younger.

31:59.418 --> 32:00.669
[inhales deeply]

32:00.752 --> 32:02.421
But you're pretty grown-up for a kid.

32:03.338 --> 32:04.464
Was that a joke?

32:05.132 --> 32:07.801
[inhales deeply]
I like you even more, Ms. Seoul.

32:07.884 --> 32:09.636
Let's shake hands. We have to.

32:09.719 --> 32:11.513
- All of a sudden?
- Yes, all of a sudden.

32:11.596 --> 32:13.098
[chuckles]

32:13.181 --> 32:14.516
[Se-jin] Nice to meet you.

32:15.100 --> 32:16.518
Let me help you.

32:20.313 --> 32:21.815
[Se-jin] I'll go start the car.

32:21.898 --> 32:23.942
- [Mi-rae] Okay.
- [Mi-ji] Hey.

32:24.025 --> 32:25.235
Hey, you.

32:25.318 --> 32:26.653
So what is it?

32:26.736 --> 32:28.905
Why did you make me come?

32:29.614 --> 32:30.657
To end it.

32:31.616 --> 32:32.617
End what?

32:32.701 --> 32:34.327
You stay here now.

32:35.203 --> 32:36.705
I'm going back to Seoul.

32:37.998 --> 32:40.333
Wait. Hold on.

32:40.417 --> 32:42.461
Just like that?

32:42.544 --> 32:44.838
Ho-su is here too, you know.

32:44.921 --> 32:46.965
If we switch back now and get caught…

32:47.048 --> 32:49.843
You dummy. Ho-su knows.

32:49.926 --> 32:52.053
He came down knowing we switched.

32:53.138 --> 32:54.556
- What?
- [rising chime]

32:54.639 --> 32:55.724
[sighs]

32:55.807 --> 32:57.809
- [quirky music playing]
- I told you not to meet him.

32:57.893 --> 32:59.394
Why did you?

32:59.478 --> 33:01.062
No, I…

33:01.146 --> 33:03.899
[sighs] Forget it. We'll talk at home.

33:03.982 --> 33:05.025
I mean…

33:05.525 --> 33:06.610
[sighs]

33:09.738 --> 33:11.031
[sighs]

33:11.114 --> 33:13.492
Ho-su knew everything?

33:13.575 --> 33:15.827
I was thinking of getting you
and Mi-ji together.

33:15.911 --> 33:17.537
- [coughs]
- You said she's your first love.

33:17.621 --> 33:20.749
Apparently,
she has something to say to you.

33:21.249 --> 33:23.919
Seriously,
what would you two do without me?

33:24.794 --> 33:26.379
This is so embarrassing.

33:26.463 --> 33:28.507
[breathes deeply, whimpers]

33:28.590 --> 33:30.800
- Where's Mi-ji?
- What? Over there.

33:31.301 --> 33:32.385
She's going to the farm.

33:36.598 --> 33:38.099
You're going home, right?

33:39.601 --> 33:41.186
Yes, home.

33:41.269 --> 33:43.021
When are you going
to the hospital tomorrow?

33:43.104 --> 33:44.731
I might go in the morning.

33:46.066 --> 33:47.192
Uh…

33:48.068 --> 33:51.071
I'm not sure. I'll talk to her.

33:51.154 --> 33:52.322
What?

33:52.405 --> 33:54.241
[music concludes]

33:56.993 --> 33:58.370
- Uh…
- [tender music playing]

33:58.453 --> 33:59.538
I…

33:59.621 --> 34:03.333
I'll talk to Mi-ji later and decide.

34:07.712 --> 34:09.714
[quirky music continues]

34:14.803 --> 34:17.931
[crying] Crap. This is mortifying.

34:18.014 --> 34:19.933
He knows everything. Why did I say Mi-ji?

34:20.016 --> 34:22.936
I'm too embarrassed to see him again!

34:23.019 --> 34:25.480
[cries]

34:25.981 --> 34:29.234
I want to crawl into a hole.

34:29.317 --> 34:31.403
[music fades]

34:40.870 --> 34:42.914
[gentle music playing]

34:42.998 --> 34:45.041
[student 1] Guys, I saw Mi-ji earlier.

34:45.125 --> 34:46.626
- [student 2] What?
- [student 3] Really?

34:46.710 --> 34:49.045
- [indistinct chatter]
- [gentle music continues]

34:57.679 --> 34:59.931
[Bun-hong] Ho-su, there you are!

35:00.015 --> 35:01.308
CONGRATULATIONS, GRADUATES!

35:01.433 --> 35:02.559
Are you Mi-rae or Mi-ji?

35:03.101 --> 35:04.978
- [young Mi-rae] I'm Mi-ji.
- Good.

35:05.061 --> 35:07.689
The two of you
should take a picture together.

35:07.772 --> 35:09.024
Go stand next to her.

35:14.237 --> 35:16.364
All right. One, two, three.

35:17.032 --> 35:19.242
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [Bun-hong] One more.

35:19.326 --> 35:20.452
[chuckles]

35:20.535 --> 35:22.203
- Congratulations.
- [young Mi-rae] Thank you.

35:22.287 --> 35:23.204
Sure.

35:27.584 --> 35:30.629
What do I have to do to see Mi-ji?

35:36.635 --> 35:39.220
[young Mi-rae]
I haven't seen much of her lately either.

35:39.304 --> 35:42.599
Ever since she got hurt,
she hardly leaves her room.

35:43.391 --> 35:46.227
I guess she doesn't want to see anyone.

35:46.311 --> 35:48.563
[gentle music continues]

36:00.492 --> 36:03.244
[music concludes]

36:06.039 --> 36:08.792
I said I'd give you a ride,
not put you to work.

36:11.127 --> 36:12.337
I'm feeling generous.

36:12.420 --> 36:15.048
You get a special bonus today.

36:16.633 --> 36:17.676
It's fine.

36:18.510 --> 36:21.971
I just wanted to help out
as a thank-you for everything.

36:22.722 --> 36:25.058
You sound like you're saying goodbye.

36:25.975 --> 36:27.310
What is it?

36:27.394 --> 36:29.813
Are you finally leaving
to chase your dreams?

36:30.814 --> 36:33.191
If anything, I'm waking up from them.

36:35.110 --> 36:36.277
[Se-jin] Hmm.

36:36.903 --> 36:39.572
By the way, Ms. Seoul was really nice.

36:40.073 --> 36:42.367
From what I'd heard,
I thought she'd be super uptight,

36:42.450 --> 36:43.743
but she was easygoing.

36:43.827 --> 36:45.662
That's rare for someone so bookish.

36:46.162 --> 36:47.288
I like her.

36:48.039 --> 36:49.249
Everyone does.

36:49.332 --> 36:53.128
Especially that look she gave me,
like, "Don't hit on my sister."

36:53.211 --> 36:54.713
[exhales] I loved it.

36:55.505 --> 36:57.841
You can't use your family
as an excuse anymore.

36:59.843 --> 37:01.428
Ms. Seoul looked like

37:01.511 --> 37:04.931
the type who'd keep a lookout
if her partner was robbing a store.

37:05.014 --> 37:07.392
Your family isn't worried,
but you are for no reason.

37:07.475 --> 37:09.144
Why not just do what you want?

37:09.227 --> 37:11.312
[sighs] Why do you keep saying that?

37:12.147 --> 37:13.106
What do you mean?

37:13.189 --> 37:15.275
Since yesterday,
you've been saying I'm making excuses.

37:15.358 --> 37:18.027
You've never lived my life,
so why are you judging me?

37:18.737 --> 37:22.031
Not everyone can live like you, Se-jin.

37:22.615 --> 37:25.994
Family, debt…
They may sound like lame excuses to you,

37:26.077 --> 37:29.080
but to me, they're real and unavoidable.

37:30.165 --> 37:31.249
[sighs]

37:31.332 --> 37:34.294
I know. I've said all those things before.

37:35.545 --> 37:37.172
[gentle music playing]

37:37.922 --> 37:39.048
Back in high school,

37:39.674 --> 37:42.635
I randomly started studying
for the civil service exam.

37:42.719 --> 37:44.220
I didn't want to study abroad.

37:45.138 --> 37:48.183
I would've failed anyway.
There were too many technical terms.

37:49.100 --> 37:51.895
But one day, Grandfather came
to the exam-prep center

37:51.978 --> 37:53.730
and asked what I was doing there.

37:53.813 --> 37:55.106
I gave the usual script.

37:55.190 --> 37:57.650
[imitating crying voice]
"You've sacrificed everything for me."

37:57.734 --> 37:59.903
"How can I just think about myself?"

37:59.986 --> 38:01.362
"We've got debts."

38:02.030 --> 38:03.907
"And I'm the only family you have."

38:04.491 --> 38:08.244
Then he yelled,
which was totally out of character.

38:09.579 --> 38:12.040
He said those weren't the real reasons,

38:12.123 --> 38:14.375
and that they were just excuses.

38:15.210 --> 38:16.211
Then…

38:16.836 --> 38:18.505
what was the real reason?

38:19.464 --> 38:20.507
I was scared.

38:21.049 --> 38:23.134
Everyone assumed I'd do well,

38:23.843 --> 38:25.678
as if that were a given.

38:26.471 --> 38:28.348
2014 GENERAL ADMISSION RESULTS

38:30.225 --> 38:32.143
YOU ARE NOT ON THE ADMISSION LIST

38:32.227 --> 38:33.978
[gentle music continues]

38:35.563 --> 38:36.606
[sighs]

38:40.616 --> 38:43.196
WISHING YOU SUCCESS IN 2019
CHEONGGIL EXAM-PREP CENTER

38:43.279 --> 38:45.031
CIVIL SERVICE EXAM
PASS LIST

38:45.114 --> 38:46.574
[gentle music continues]

38:46.658 --> 38:48.284
REGISTRATION NUMBER: 100012486

38:57.293 --> 38:58.545
[sighs]

39:00.213 --> 39:02.090
[music turns pensive]

39:12.350 --> 39:13.589
EXAM QUESTIONS

39:18.648 --> 39:20.733
[Se-jin] I was afraid
of not meeting expectations…

39:20.817 --> 39:21.693
[Mi-rae sighs]

39:21.776 --> 39:24.153
…and of disappointing myself.

39:24.237 --> 39:26.698
The fact that nothing was certain
made me anxious.

39:27.866 --> 39:30.785
And I was scared
I'd feel that way forever.

39:31.995 --> 39:34.581
But those reasons are silly.

39:34.664 --> 39:38.459
What fool doesn't scratch a lottery ticket
just because it might be a dud?

39:38.543 --> 39:39.627
Hey…

39:42.046 --> 39:43.673
are you that fool?

39:49.512 --> 39:51.055
[soft pensive music continues]

39:59.814 --> 40:01.190
[Se-jin] Think about it.

40:01.274 --> 40:03.568
What's the real reason you're hesitating?

40:14.746 --> 40:16.456
[music concludes]

40:17.081 --> 40:18.583
Hey, you.

40:20.376 --> 40:23.129
It's been ages
since we last shared a room.

40:23.212 --> 40:24.756
Close the door.

40:24.839 --> 40:26.299
You're going to bed already?

40:26.841 --> 40:29.385
You said we'd talk at home.

40:30.637 --> 40:33.014
Do you really want to go
to Seoul tomorrow?

40:33.723 --> 40:36.059
What are you going to do with your hair?

40:36.684 --> 40:38.227
We'll talk tomorrow.

40:39.187 --> 40:40.313
Tomorrow?

40:40.396 --> 40:41.940
What about work?

40:42.815 --> 40:45.568
I'll take a day off,
so let's talk tomorrow.

40:46.569 --> 40:48.947
I'm going to sleep. Close the door.

40:49.030 --> 40:50.198
[Mi-ji] Mm.

41:06.130 --> 41:07.340
[exhales]

41:10.510 --> 41:12.595
[Mi-ji] Come on.

41:12.679 --> 41:16.766
Can't you just go to the hospital?
I'll go to the Youth Association thing.

41:17.266 --> 41:21.062
I, Mi-rae, came from Seoul
just to help with typhoon recovery work?

41:21.604 --> 41:24.148
Then does Mi-rae have to go
to the hospital?

41:24.232 --> 41:26.818
Didn't you say Mom's not even that hurt?

41:26.901 --> 41:30.488
Mi-rae could just call Mom
and visit Grandma…

41:30.571 --> 41:32.573
If I took a day off, came home,

41:32.657 --> 41:34.659
and went back without even seeing Mom,

41:34.742 --> 41:36.661
what does that make me?

41:37.161 --> 41:40.248
[sighs] Go. Don't make me a bad daughter.

41:43.751 --> 41:46.337
- [whines, grumbles]
- [door closes]

41:49.007 --> 41:50.174
[gate closes]

41:52.051 --> 41:54.804
You're not waiting for me, right?
Mi-ji will be out soon.

41:54.887 --> 41:55.930
Mi-rae.

41:57.724 --> 42:00.476
- We didn't get to finish our chat.
- [Mi-rae] Later.

42:01.185 --> 42:03.396
I'll call you when I'm done with work.

42:03.479 --> 42:04.689
One more thing.

42:06.774 --> 42:07.775
Thank you.

42:09.277 --> 42:10.987
For not telling Mi-ji yesterday.

42:11.821 --> 42:13.406
You could've just told her.

42:14.282 --> 42:15.533
I did tell her.

42:17.410 --> 42:19.787
[intriguing quirky music playing]

42:22.832 --> 42:23.833
Oh my!

42:23.916 --> 42:25.001
Gosh.

42:26.419 --> 42:27.962
Shoot, I…

42:28.046 --> 42:29.297
forgot something.

42:29.380 --> 42:30.882
- [Ho-su] Oh, you did?
- Yes.

42:31.799 --> 42:33.968
You can go get it. I'll wait here.

42:34.052 --> 42:36.929
No, it might take a while.

42:37.013 --> 42:39.098
- You go ahead.
- Okay…

42:39.182 --> 42:40.349
[gate opens]

42:41.642 --> 42:42.518
[music concludes]

42:42.602 --> 42:45.063
[Bun-hong]
How did you know it was so dry in here?

42:45.605 --> 42:48.066
How thoughtful of you
to bring a humidifier.

42:48.983 --> 42:51.486
We'll be here for one night.
Isn't this a bit much?

42:51.569 --> 42:55.406
What's "a bit much" is you
hanging wet towels all over the place.

42:56.783 --> 42:59.160
- Hi, Mi-rae.
- [Mi-ji] Hello.

42:59.911 --> 43:02.371
Oh my, Mi-rae. What brings you here?

43:02.455 --> 43:03.414
Did you come alone?

43:03.498 --> 43:06.501
Yes, Mi-ji went
to the Youth Association thing.

43:06.584 --> 43:09.837
[Bun-hong] Oh, Mi-rae,
how long has it been?

43:09.921 --> 43:11.798
You've gotten even prettier.

43:11.881 --> 43:13.883
It's been a while
since you saw Ho-su, right?

43:13.966 --> 43:14.926
Yes.

43:15.676 --> 43:18.054
- Hi.
- Hello.

43:19.430 --> 43:21.557
You didn't have to come. I'm out tomorrow.

43:21.641 --> 43:23.017
You must be busy with work.

43:23.101 --> 43:24.727
And what's this?

43:24.811 --> 43:25.978
- Just a few things…
- Oh dear.

43:26.062 --> 43:27.772
…I thought you might need.

43:27.855 --> 43:29.857
This might be a bit much, but…

43:30.900 --> 43:33.027
What do you mean?

43:33.111 --> 43:35.113
It was dry in here, so this is perfect.

43:35.196 --> 43:36.405
[chuckles]

43:36.489 --> 43:38.825
It's like Mi-rae and Ho-su are in sync.

43:39.867 --> 43:42.495
They say it takes brains
to be considerate.

43:42.578 --> 43:47.375
That could be why
you're both so thoughtful. [chuckles]

43:47.458 --> 43:48.584
[quirky music playing]

43:48.668 --> 43:51.254
[Bun-hong] Maybe it's because
I haven't seen you in a while,

43:51.337 --> 43:53.631
but you and Mi-ji used to look identical.

43:54.132 --> 43:56.551
Now that you're older,
I can finally tell who's who.

43:57.510 --> 43:59.470
- Really?
- [Bun-hong] Yes.

43:59.554 --> 44:02.557
Mi-rae looks like a real lady now.

44:03.141 --> 44:06.102
Mi-ji still seems like a kid. [chuckles]

44:06.185 --> 44:07.603
- Mom.
- [chuckles]

44:10.189 --> 44:16.863
Mi-rae just has this calm,
intelligent vibe, you know?

44:16.946 --> 44:17.905
[Ok-hui chuckles]

44:17.989 --> 44:20.700
So she's more than
just an acquaintance, unlike Mi-ji?

44:20.783 --> 44:22.827
Why bring that up in front of the kids?

44:24.120 --> 44:26.122
[Mi-ji] What is it? Is your back itchy?

44:26.205 --> 44:28.916
It's probably because I haven't showered.

44:29.000 --> 44:31.002
Your skin must be dry.
I'll put some moisturizer on.

44:31.085 --> 44:33.546
It's fine. I'll do it myself later.

44:33.629 --> 44:35.464
[Mi-ji] You can't put it
on your back yourself.

44:35.548 --> 44:37.800
- No, it's fine.
- Let me.

44:37.884 --> 44:40.469
- [Ok-hui] I'll do it myself.
- [Mi-ji] Just stay still.

44:40.553 --> 44:42.722
- [Ok-hui] Jeez.
- [Mi-ji] Let me see.

44:43.264 --> 44:46.058
[gasps] It's all red already.

44:49.061 --> 44:52.398
It's just a bit of a scratch.
There's no need for you to stay here.

44:52.899 --> 44:54.150
Go back to Seoul.

44:54.233 --> 44:56.277
I should at least see Grandma
since I'm here.

44:56.360 --> 44:57.653
Mi-rae.

44:59.155 --> 45:01.073
If you see Grandma,

45:01.574 --> 45:03.201
don't mention that I got hurt.

45:03.868 --> 45:05.661
Why? Because she'll worry?

45:05.745 --> 45:08.206
[chuckles] Goodness. Worried?

45:08.706 --> 45:11.292
Your grandma's not the type
to worry about me.

45:11.375 --> 45:13.044
- No, a bit higher.
- Higher?

45:13.127 --> 45:15.796
- Here?
- Yes, that's the spot. [chuckles]

45:15.880 --> 45:19.634
She's only sweet to you kids, not to me.

45:19.717 --> 45:22.637
If she hears I got hurt,
she'll nag at me for not acting my age.

45:23.387 --> 45:25.473
Anyway, go back to Seoul.

45:25.556 --> 45:28.851
It's just a minor scratch.
Besides, you're busy.

45:28.935 --> 45:31.979
What are you talking about?
You're lucky it wasn't worse.

45:32.980 --> 45:34.398
All done.

45:39.195 --> 45:41.489
Uh, I'll go get some water
for the humidifier.

45:41.572 --> 45:43.115
- I'll do it.
- [Mi-ji] Let me.

45:43.199 --> 45:44.909
- I've got it.
- [Mi-ji] I can do it.

45:46.452 --> 45:47.703
[Ok-hui sighs]

45:47.787 --> 45:50.873
She's being unusually sweet.

45:51.916 --> 45:55.628
Of course she is. You got hurt,
and she hasn't seen you in ages.

45:55.711 --> 45:59.966
Are you seriously complaining
about your daughter being sweet to you?

46:00.758 --> 46:02.468
Who's complaining?

46:02.551 --> 46:04.553
I was just saying
she's being unusually sweet, right?

46:04.637 --> 46:05.554
[Bun-hong chuckles]

46:05.638 --> 46:10.142
[Ok-hui] Your mom really knows how
to get under people's skin with a smile.

46:24.323 --> 46:25.324
You go first.

46:26.033 --> 46:26.993
[Ho-su] Okay.

46:31.289 --> 46:32.206
Thanks.

46:44.677 --> 46:46.095
Are you mad at me?

46:46.178 --> 46:49.724
[scoffs] Why would I be mad at you?

46:49.807 --> 46:51.475
Then why are you

46:51.559 --> 46:53.185
avoiding my eyes?

46:53.269 --> 46:54.186
[scoffs]

46:54.770 --> 46:57.023
Don't be absurd.

46:57.815 --> 46:59.692
When did I…

47:00.401 --> 47:02.486
[tender music playing]

47:04.739 --> 47:05.906
Can you believe Mi-ji?

47:05.990 --> 47:08.868
She's off to the Youth Association thing
when Mom is hurt.

47:09.493 --> 47:11.787
- She even made me take a day off.
- [water running]

47:11.871 --> 47:13.831
No job, no worries, right?

47:15.291 --> 47:16.250
- You…
- [water stops]

47:16.334 --> 47:19.045
The tank is full. I'll head in first.

47:19.128 --> 47:21.047
Wait, I…

47:23.382 --> 47:24.383
[sighs]

47:25.426 --> 47:27.178
She is avoiding me.

47:27.261 --> 47:28.554
[music fades]

47:28.637 --> 47:31.223
[Myeong-gap] Okay, let's wrap things up.

47:31.307 --> 47:32.725
Thanks for all your hard work.

47:32.808 --> 47:33.934
DUSON-RI SENIOR CENTER

47:34.018 --> 47:37.355
There's some boiled pork at the town hall.

47:37.438 --> 47:40.232
If you want some, come on in.

47:40.316 --> 47:42.818
If not, you can go home.

47:42.902 --> 47:45.446
Do as you please, okay?

47:45.529 --> 47:47.948
[Il-lam] Are you telling us
to come or not?

47:48.032 --> 47:50.368
- [Myeong-gap] I'm telling you to leave.
- [both laugh]

47:52.495 --> 47:54.705
- [Myeong-gap] Hey, Il-lam…
- You're not going?

47:55.373 --> 47:57.416
No, I'm not.

47:59.585 --> 48:01.420
Now it really feels like the end.

48:03.547 --> 48:04.882
All right, then.

48:10.554 --> 48:11.806
Uh…

48:13.265 --> 48:15.184
- Okay.
- Goodbye.

48:15.267 --> 48:16.394
Mi-rae.

48:21.148 --> 48:22.483
[Mi-rae] Hey, wait.

48:25.069 --> 48:28.447
Can you tell me now instead of tomorrow?

48:28.531 --> 48:30.157
The real reason you quit?

48:32.535 --> 48:34.412
There's still half a day left.

48:37.665 --> 48:40.209
I guess we might not
see each other tomorrow.

48:40.292 --> 48:41.919
[breathes deeply]

48:43.712 --> 48:46.674
Follow me.
We need a drink for this conversation.

48:57.059 --> 48:59.228
Have you heard of Neo Trading Company?

49:00.187 --> 49:01.105
[Mi-rae] Of course.

49:01.188 --> 49:04.150
You replaced the management there
and then suddenly vanished.

49:04.233 --> 49:06.652
[chuckles softly] So you know.

49:08.696 --> 49:11.866
Actually, I forced my way into that deal.

49:13.451 --> 49:15.870
There was this investor
who had two percent of the shares,

49:15.953 --> 49:17.830
and everyone at my company went all in.

49:17.913 --> 49:21.041
We were dead set on convincing him

49:21.125 --> 49:23.669
and talked until our mouths went dry.

49:23.752 --> 49:26.297
Yes, we've secured enough for attendance.

49:26.380 --> 49:28.799
We just need two percent
of the voting rights.

49:30.718 --> 49:33.304
All those chronic issues
you've complained about?

49:33.387 --> 49:34.972
We could finally fix them for good.

49:35.055 --> 49:36.390
[cell phone buzzing]

49:38.017 --> 49:40.603
[Se-jin] Then my grandfather called.

49:40.686 --> 49:42.354
- He never used to call me.
- [buzzing stops]

49:42.438 --> 49:44.356
- So we think…
- I didn't answer.

49:44.440 --> 49:47.026
…replacing the management
is the only solution.

49:47.109 --> 49:49.403
We have a solid list of candidates
for the board,

49:49.487 --> 49:51.614
so if you could
really get behind us this time…

49:51.697 --> 49:52.740
[cell phone buzzing]

49:52.823 --> 49:53.824
Excuse me.

49:53.908 --> 49:56.494
- Then he called again.
- [coworker] Hey.

49:56.577 --> 49:58.120
[Se-jin] What do I do?

49:58.204 --> 50:00.206
This conference call
has life-or-death stakes.

50:00.289 --> 50:01.207
[buzzing stops]

50:01.290 --> 50:02.958
Sorry. Excuse me. [clears throat]

50:04.001 --> 50:07.463
Yes, we can address
your concerns at the root.

50:07.546 --> 50:11.425
We plan to reduce low-profit businesses
handled by minor subsidiaries…

50:11.509 --> 50:12.843
That's when he passed away.

50:13.594 --> 50:15.888
From heatstroke,
in the middle of his farm.

50:17.139 --> 50:18.098
[softly] Oh.

50:18.182 --> 50:20.976
[Se-jin] The call
with life-or-death stakes was his.

50:22.770 --> 50:24.522
After he died…

50:25.981 --> 50:27.191
I felt like…

50:28.067 --> 50:29.151
something inside me…

50:30.694 --> 50:33.155
just collapsed and fell apart.

50:36.742 --> 50:40.037
But not everyone reacts that way
to death, you know?

50:40.120 --> 50:42.206
They go to work. They eat.

50:44.083 --> 50:45.417
But I couldn't.

50:47.419 --> 50:48.796
That's why I quit.

50:49.880 --> 50:51.257
[gentle music playing]

50:51.340 --> 50:53.592
I didn't know what part of me was broken.

50:54.885 --> 50:56.804
And I was scared I'd fall apart again.

50:58.222 --> 51:00.015
It's not as dramatic as the rumors.

51:03.686 --> 51:06.522
Don't the rumors bother you?

51:07.189 --> 51:10.276
Everyone assumed they were true
since you disappeared so suddenly.

51:12.069 --> 51:14.321
Should I have stuck it out a bit longer?

51:15.489 --> 51:16.490
No.

51:17.157 --> 51:19.660
There's no point proving
something that isn't true.

51:20.202 --> 51:23.372
If the people by your side
know the truth, that's enough.

51:26.041 --> 51:27.126
By the way,

51:28.085 --> 51:30.212
why'd you say you'd tell me tomorrow?

51:30.296 --> 51:31.171
[Se-jin] Oh, that.

51:32.089 --> 51:33.507
Tomorrow is his birthday.

51:34.425 --> 51:36.552
Perfect timing
for a trip down memory lane.

51:38.679 --> 51:41.557
He was always so gruff,
but he loved the stars.

51:42.433 --> 51:43.892
At midnight on my birthday,

51:43.976 --> 51:47.146
he'd pack seaweed soup in a thermos
and take me stargazing.

51:47.229 --> 51:50.983
He said the sky was full of stars
the night I was born.

51:53.777 --> 51:56.655
Now I celebrate his birthday alone
doing the same thing.

51:57.489 --> 51:58.699
What a fool I am.

52:00.034 --> 52:01.118
Cheers.

52:05.372 --> 52:06.498
[Se-jin slurps]

52:15.424 --> 52:17.509
[music fades]

52:33.525 --> 52:34.526
Grandma!

52:43.327 --> 52:44.370
You're here.

52:45.162 --> 52:47.247
[squeals]

52:47.331 --> 52:50.459
- Grandma! [cries joyfully]
- [tender music playing]

52:50.542 --> 52:52.628
- [chuckles]
- How have you been?

52:53.837 --> 52:54.963
[Wol-sun] Oh, oh.

52:55.047 --> 52:58.217
- [Mi-ji grunting softly]
- [Wol-sun] Goodness me.

52:58.300 --> 52:59.718
BONGDEOK HOSPITAL

52:59.802 --> 53:04.014
Is it all over now?

53:04.098 --> 53:07.017
I don't know. I can't tell if it is.

53:07.601 --> 53:11.105
We said we'd end it once Mi-rae was okay,

53:11.188 --> 53:13.607
but I'm not sure she is.

53:14.108 --> 53:16.151
Mm! My mom saw me with this hair.

53:16.777 --> 53:19.029
Did you tell your mom?

53:19.113 --> 53:21.156
- [music fades]
- What, that we switched?

53:21.240 --> 53:22.282
[Wol-sun] Yes.

53:22.366 --> 53:24.576
What's the point in telling Mom?

53:24.660 --> 53:27.454
She'd say I'm ruining Mi-rae's life
and scold me.

53:27.538 --> 53:29.415
I came because she got hurt.

53:29.498 --> 53:30.999
She's hurt?

53:31.834 --> 53:34.044
It's nothing serious.

53:34.128 --> 53:37.047
She was squabbling with Bun-hong
and got a little scraped up.

53:37.131 --> 53:38.090
Where?

53:38.757 --> 53:42.511
Tell your mom to come here now.

53:42.594 --> 53:45.305
She can't. She's in the hospital.

53:46.056 --> 53:48.809
It's not that serious.
She's just there for some tests.

53:49.601 --> 53:52.312
Let's go to your mom.

53:52.396 --> 53:53.772
- To Mom?
- [Wol-sun] Yes.

53:53.856 --> 53:55.149
You can't go.

53:55.232 --> 53:57.735
I'll take the wheelchair.

53:57.818 --> 53:58.986
Come on.

53:59.069 --> 54:01.530
Let's go see your mom.

54:01.613 --> 54:05.743
Grandma, I'll tell Mom to come
as soon as she's discharged.

54:05.826 --> 54:07.619
Don't worry, okay?

54:07.703 --> 54:09.788
- [whimpers]
- She'll be fine.

54:15.335 --> 54:16.545
[Wol-sun whimpers]

54:20.132 --> 54:22.593
Here's the information
you requested on Kim Ro-sa.

54:25.095 --> 54:28.849
It appears she grew up
in an orphanage and has no relatives

54:28.932 --> 54:30.559
except for a son.

54:30.642 --> 54:32.978
What about her husband?
There must be a father.

54:33.061 --> 54:35.272
According to a contact
at the prosecutor's office,

54:35.355 --> 54:37.858
he was murdered.
By someone Kim Ro-sa knew.

54:37.941 --> 54:39.318
- What?
- [intriguing music playing]

54:39.401 --> 54:41.028
Was it a crime of passion?

54:41.111 --> 54:43.238
No, the defendant was a woman.

54:43.322 --> 54:45.783
She was also from the same orphanage.

54:45.866 --> 54:47.201
No prior criminal record.

54:47.284 --> 54:51.246
Ms. Kim testified on her behalf,
so she got a reduced sentence.

54:51.330 --> 54:52.623
She testified for her?

54:53.624 --> 54:55.959
Can we contact her now?

54:56.043 --> 54:58.045
It's been confirmed that she's deceased.

54:58.712 --> 54:59.838
Deceased…

55:00.380 --> 55:01.590
Look into her some more.

55:01.673 --> 55:03.801
And keep tracking Kim Ro-sa.

55:05.719 --> 55:07.137
What's her name?

55:07.221 --> 55:08.764
Hyeon Sang-wol.

55:08.847 --> 55:10.140
Hyeon…

55:10.224 --> 55:11.350
"Hyeon Sang-wol."

55:11.433 --> 55:12.768
FIRST TRIAL VERDICT

55:12.851 --> 55:14.019
Hyeon…

55:14.102 --> 55:15.187
DOMESTIC VIOLENCE

55:15.270 --> 55:17.064
[muttering] …Sang-wol…

55:17.147 --> 55:18.232
[music builds]

55:18.315 --> 55:20.192
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
HYEON SANG-WOL

55:20.275 --> 55:21.819
DATE OF BIRTH: FEB 14, 1955

55:21.902 --> 55:23.487
[music concludes]

55:23.570 --> 55:25.614
[Ro-sa] No need to be sorry.

55:25.697 --> 55:27.825
You went home
because your mother got hurt.

55:28.534 --> 55:31.870
[Ho-su] Still, I should have met you
in person and told you how it went.

55:31.954 --> 55:34.122
There's nothing much to tell.

55:34.206 --> 55:36.333
You declined because I told you to.

55:36.875 --> 55:39.127
So is the whole thing over?

55:39.211 --> 55:40.546
[Ho-su] Uh…

55:40.629 --> 55:41.797
Ms. Ro-sa.

55:43.340 --> 55:45.551
Can I ask you something?

55:45.634 --> 55:47.970
Sure. What is it?

55:48.053 --> 55:49.137
[Ho-su] Before,

55:49.221 --> 55:52.641
I never got to ask
why you're not selling the building.

55:52.724 --> 55:53.851
[Ro-sa] I told you.

55:53.934 --> 55:56.895
I hate anything complicated,
money included.

55:58.021 --> 55:59.731
Is there…

56:01.525 --> 56:02.901
any other reason?

56:02.985 --> 56:04.820
What do you mean?

56:06.280 --> 56:07.364
Before,

56:08.031 --> 56:12.244
I figured it might be personal,
so I didn't dig any deeper.

56:12.911 --> 56:17.249
But if there's a specific reason
that's keeping you from selling,

56:17.332 --> 56:20.294
I'm pretty sure I can help.

56:20.377 --> 56:22.004
- [pensive music playing]
- [sighs]

56:22.087 --> 56:25.257
You're not making any sense.

56:26.174 --> 56:29.469
Isn't your job done now?

56:30.178 --> 56:32.347
I'm not asking
as your legal representative.

56:33.140 --> 56:34.641
This is a personal question.

56:36.810 --> 56:39.855
I offered to help,
but all I did was pass along messages.

56:40.564 --> 56:42.983
I feel like I haven't been of much help.

56:43.609 --> 56:47.154
If you're worried that the paperwork
or procedures are complicated,

56:47.237 --> 56:48.989
I can handle it for you.

56:49.072 --> 56:51.158
Or anything else, just say the word…

56:51.241 --> 56:53.327
There's nothing to help with.

56:54.578 --> 56:56.371
It's all over now, right?

56:57.831 --> 56:58.707
Yes.

56:58.790 --> 57:00.834
- [doorbell chimes]
- Oh, I've got customers.

57:00.918 --> 57:03.378
Come by for a meal sometime.

57:06.715 --> 57:08.342
[customer] Hello!

57:08.425 --> 57:09.635
Hi, ma'am.

57:09.718 --> 57:12.179
The chicken giblet stew here is amazing.

57:17.517 --> 57:19.269
[pensive music continues]

57:23.065 --> 57:24.232
[sighs heavily]

57:26.818 --> 57:28.195
[doorbell rings]

57:28.904 --> 57:30.906
[music fades]

57:50.968 --> 57:53.053
Sorry I snapped yesterday.

57:53.887 --> 57:55.847
You came to help, after all.

57:57.015 --> 57:58.016
It's fine.

57:58.517 --> 58:00.102
I showed up out of the blue.

58:02.938 --> 58:04.773
The last time I saw you…

58:06.692 --> 58:08.068
You're right. I ran away.

58:09.569 --> 58:11.029
Seeing your face…

58:12.155 --> 58:14.157
made me think about my family.

58:15.867 --> 58:19.705
I didn't want them
to find out about my problems.

58:21.039 --> 58:23.041
It's something I have to fix myself.

58:23.709 --> 58:25.419
You don't have to do it alone.

58:27.212 --> 58:30.757
If you're uncomfortable with me,
I can refer you to another lawyer.

58:31.258 --> 58:34.511
Or we can find other ways
outside the legal route.

58:34.594 --> 58:36.471
- Maybe--
- I appreciate it.

58:37.848 --> 58:38.974
But honestly,

58:40.058 --> 58:43.520
I don't even know what kind of help
to ask for right now.

58:44.813 --> 58:46.773
I'll go back, see what I need,

58:46.857 --> 58:50.652
and let you know if I need any help.

59:00.495 --> 59:02.372
[quirky music playing]

59:05.333 --> 59:06.334
[mouths] Man…

59:06.418 --> 59:08.295
Oh. Mi-rae!

59:12.007 --> 59:13.717
- Hi.
- [Gyeong-gu] Hey.

59:16.178 --> 59:17.262
[Gyeong-gu chuckles]

59:20.140 --> 59:22.017
Long time no see.

59:22.809 --> 59:24.311
- I know.
- [Gyeong-gu] Yeah.

59:24.394 --> 59:25.395
[chuckles]

59:26.855 --> 59:28.648
You must be busy. What brings you here?

59:28.732 --> 59:31.318
A family matter.

59:32.027 --> 59:33.070
I see.

59:33.153 --> 59:34.321
[Mi-ji] Yes.

59:35.447 --> 59:36.865
Where's Mi-ji?

59:37.407 --> 59:38.825
Mi-ji?

59:38.909 --> 59:40.285
She's at home.

59:40.368 --> 59:42.287
- Home?
- [Mi-ji] Yes.

59:42.913 --> 59:43.914
[Gyeong-gu] Mm.

59:43.997 --> 59:45.874
At home, my foot!

59:45.957 --> 59:47.667
You're seriously asking for it, Mi-ji.

59:47.751 --> 59:49.878
Hey! Why did you pretend you didn't know?

59:49.961 --> 59:52.339
You're one to talk!
Why didn't you call me?

59:52.422 --> 59:55.217
- You're my only friend.
- What about me? You're all I've got.

59:55.300 --> 59:57.928
I was losing my mind
not being able to reach out to you.

59:58.011 --> 59:59.930
Jeez… Hey.

01:00:00.847 --> 01:00:03.850
- Look.
- [gasps] Hamcheol?

01:00:03.934 --> 01:00:05.352
- [squeals]
- [laughs]

01:00:05.435 --> 01:00:07.604
I never got to show anyone.

01:00:07.687 --> 01:00:09.815
- It's cute, right?
- You got it there? Cute!

01:00:09.898 --> 01:00:11.108
GYEONG-GU MART

01:00:11.191 --> 01:00:13.068
- [music fades]
- At the wedding?

01:00:13.735 --> 01:00:17.197
Ho-su's always been that way.
Nothing can stop him when he's fired up.

01:00:17.906 --> 01:00:19.032
That's badass.

01:00:20.242 --> 01:00:23.245
But how did you run into him
in a huge city like Seoul?

01:00:23.328 --> 01:00:24.913
That's fate, if you ask me.

01:00:26.206 --> 01:00:27.415
Hey, Gyeong-gu.

01:00:28.291 --> 01:00:29.793
Did you know…

01:00:30.961 --> 01:00:32.629
that Ho-su--

01:00:32.712 --> 01:00:33.964
Liked you?

01:00:34.840 --> 01:00:37.551
I figured after my love confession stunt.

01:00:38.135 --> 01:00:41.471
But you didn't really say anything,
so I thought you turned him down.

01:00:41.555 --> 01:00:43.431
[soft quirky music playing]

01:00:44.432 --> 01:00:46.309
You've got a weird look on your face.

01:00:48.436 --> 01:00:50.147
Do you like Ho-su?

01:00:50.230 --> 01:00:51.314
I don't know.

01:00:51.398 --> 01:00:53.150
Oh my. That's crazy!

01:00:53.233 --> 01:00:54.943
That hurts.

01:00:55.026 --> 01:00:56.236
Since when?

01:00:56.319 --> 01:00:58.864
Did something happen in Seoul?
Or back in high school?

01:00:58.947 --> 01:01:01.074
Nothing happened.

01:01:01.158 --> 01:01:03.743
I only just found out
I was his first love.

01:01:03.827 --> 01:01:06.037
If you heard that, then it's settled.

01:01:06.121 --> 01:01:08.331
If a guy calls you his first love,

01:01:08.415 --> 01:01:10.250
you've basically won the game.

01:01:10.333 --> 01:01:11.710
Forget it.

01:01:11.793 --> 01:01:15.547
First love or not,
it was before I got injured.

01:01:15.630 --> 01:01:17.716
- [music fades]
- Why does that matter?

01:01:17.799 --> 01:01:20.218
- Did he like you for your ankle?
- Come on.

01:01:21.845 --> 01:01:26.308
We saw each other
the day before he left for Seoul.

01:01:27.058 --> 01:01:29.477
Back then, I was in a really bad place.

01:01:29.561 --> 01:01:32.147
I was blaming myself
and everyone around me.

01:01:32.731 --> 01:01:34.191
[knocking on door]

01:01:35.400 --> 01:01:36.735
[young Mi-rae] Mi-ji.

01:01:39.988 --> 01:01:42.032
Ho-su is going to Seoul tomorrow.

01:01:44.868 --> 01:01:46.870
I'm leaving something outside your room.

01:01:56.087 --> 01:01:58.840
[gentle music playing]

01:02:02.052 --> 01:02:03.720
[doorknob rattling]

01:02:09.142 --> 01:02:12.020
[Ho-su] Mi-ji, I'll be waiting
outside your house tonight.

01:02:16.107 --> 01:02:19.194
[soft pensive music playing]

01:02:44.970 --> 01:02:46.096
[young Ho-su] Are you…

01:02:48.056 --> 01:02:49.224
really Mi-ji?

01:02:51.142 --> 01:02:52.143
[scoffs]

01:02:55.105 --> 01:02:56.606
- [music fades]
- Does it matter?

01:02:58.316 --> 01:03:00.110
You can't tell us apart anyway.

01:03:05.949 --> 01:03:07.492
Why did you give this to me?

01:03:10.287 --> 01:03:11.288
We…

01:03:13.373 --> 01:03:14.874
talked about this.

01:03:16.251 --> 01:03:17.460
When we go to Seoul,

01:03:18.086 --> 01:03:19.963
we'd check out these places together.

01:03:20.922 --> 01:03:22.132
[gentle music playing]

01:03:22.215 --> 01:03:25.218
- I'm leaving for Seoul first and--
- [young Mi-ji] Seriously,

01:03:25.302 --> 01:03:28.096
what's the point of giving this to me now?

01:03:28.179 --> 01:03:30.849
- To mess with me?
- No, I'm not trying to--

01:03:30.932 --> 01:03:33.310
Then do you feel sorry for me
or something?

01:03:34.436 --> 01:03:35.562
Hey.

01:03:36.396 --> 01:03:38.565
[voice trembling] How can I go to Seoul?

01:03:40.734 --> 01:03:43.528
My ankle's wrecked, and my life's ruined.

01:03:47.240 --> 01:03:48.575
It's not ruined.

01:03:51.619 --> 01:03:52.996
You'll get better.

01:03:54.956 --> 01:03:56.249
Are you a doctor?

01:03:57.584 --> 01:04:00.003
How am I ever supposed to get better?

01:04:00.086 --> 01:04:01.129
[sobs, sniffles]

01:04:01.963 --> 01:04:03.173
[exhales]

01:04:08.636 --> 01:04:11.014
Now I get why you acted out.

01:04:12.557 --> 01:04:14.309
Being pitied

01:04:15.602 --> 01:04:16.936
feels like crap.

01:04:20.273 --> 01:04:21.608
We're done here, right?

01:04:23.568 --> 01:04:24.569
Mi-ji.

01:04:26.321 --> 01:04:29.115
[gentle music continues]

01:04:44.089 --> 01:04:45.590
[gate closes]

01:04:45.673 --> 01:04:49.052
[Mi-ji] It's weird.
I said way worse things to him.

01:04:49.135 --> 01:04:51.262
But when he asked
if I was really Mi-ji,

01:04:51.346 --> 01:04:53.932
it just really stuck with me.

01:04:54.015 --> 01:04:55.141
[music fades]

01:04:55.225 --> 01:04:59.896
I thought, "The Mi-ji he knew
was the bright, happy runner."

01:05:00.647 --> 01:05:04.776
"That version of me is gone now,
so he can't recognize me anymore."

01:05:06.486 --> 01:05:09.614
So his first love was that Mi-ji,

01:05:09.697 --> 01:05:10.907
not me.

01:05:12.992 --> 01:05:14.035
Gosh.

01:05:14.577 --> 01:05:16.746
Cut the "old me, new me" crap.

01:05:16.830 --> 01:05:18.206
So what now?

01:05:19.082 --> 01:05:20.750
What are you going to do?

01:05:20.834 --> 01:05:22.001
What do you mean?

01:05:22.085 --> 01:05:24.963
You said you like Ho-su.

01:05:25.046 --> 01:05:27.257
And he knows, right?

01:05:27.340 --> 01:05:28.716
Then man up and tell him.

01:05:28.800 --> 01:05:32.804
I can't even look him in the eye.
How can I tell him?

01:05:32.887 --> 01:05:34.097
Jeez.

01:05:34.180 --> 01:05:35.807
Why can't you look at him?

01:05:35.890 --> 01:05:38.226
Does the sight of him make you go crazy?

01:05:38.309 --> 01:05:40.770
It's not that. Listen.

01:05:40.854 --> 01:05:42.939
When I was pretending to be Mi-rae,
it was fine.

01:05:43.022 --> 01:05:45.942
But as me, I don't know
how to act around him.

01:05:46.025 --> 01:05:47.902
It's like I've taken off a mask.

01:05:47.986 --> 01:05:50.363
Everything feels too real all of a sudden.

01:05:50.447 --> 01:05:52.907
What am I going to do with you,
you hopeless little virgin?

01:05:52.991 --> 01:05:55.201
- Good heavens.
- Jeez.

01:05:55.285 --> 01:05:58.079
So what now? You won't tell him?

01:05:58.163 --> 01:05:59.622
I don't know. Maybe later.

01:05:59.706 --> 01:06:01.458
When exactly is "later"?

01:06:01.541 --> 01:06:03.960
We'll be 40 before you know it.

01:06:04.043 --> 01:06:06.796
Come on. Mi-rae's going through hell.

01:06:06.880 --> 01:06:09.299
Is this really the time
to be asking him out?

01:06:10.258 --> 01:06:13.678
Whatever. I don't know.

01:06:16.598 --> 01:06:19.309
[Bun-hong] Ho-su, will you pick me up
tomorrow when I get discharged?

01:06:19.392 --> 01:06:20.768
What's wrong with this?

01:06:20.852 --> 01:06:23.855
[Bun-hong] If you do, I'll be so happy.

01:06:23.938 --> 01:06:27.108
[chuckles] Getting injured has its perks!

01:06:29.777 --> 01:06:31.654
No.

01:06:31.738 --> 01:06:34.199
I just mean that I'm happy.

01:06:34.282 --> 01:06:36.784
Okay, sleep tight.

01:06:39.120 --> 01:06:40.497
[cell phone beeps]

01:06:44.542 --> 01:06:46.878
- What?
- I'm just amazed.

01:06:47.795 --> 01:06:51.466
How can you say things like that
and not even cringe?

01:06:51.549 --> 01:06:54.344
If it pisses you off,
just close the curtain.

01:06:56.054 --> 01:06:59.641
Who said I'm pissed off?
I just said I was amazed.

01:06:59.724 --> 01:07:01.684
I can't say things like that, you know.

01:07:01.768 --> 01:07:03.853
[Bun-hong] Instead of saying you can't…

01:07:05.188 --> 01:07:07.273
why not try a little harder?

01:07:07.357 --> 01:07:09.067
What was that earlier?

01:07:09.150 --> 01:07:11.653
You hadn't seen Mi-rae in ages,
and you basically sent her away!

01:07:11.736 --> 01:07:13.738
It's not that I don't like her.

01:07:13.821 --> 01:07:16.282
Then you sent her away
because you love her?

01:07:17.534 --> 01:07:20.453
How is anyone supposed to know
what you mean when you talk like that?

01:07:20.537 --> 01:07:23.831
Even if I say things plainly,
people always take it the wrong way.

01:07:25.208 --> 01:07:26.876
You did it just now.

01:07:27.752 --> 01:07:29.504
- When?
- [Ok-hui] A moment ago.

01:07:29.587 --> 01:07:32.507
I said I was amazed,
and you assumed I was pissed off.

01:07:32.590 --> 01:07:35.009
Unbelievable. And what?

01:07:35.635 --> 01:07:37.929
You thought I was talking
about Ho-su's condition?

01:07:38.012 --> 01:07:39.222
Bun-hong.

01:07:39.305 --> 01:07:42.850
My child suffers from health problems too.
How could I ever say such a thing?

01:07:42.934 --> 01:07:46.229
What did you think of me all these years?

01:07:46.312 --> 01:07:47.397
Gosh.

01:07:48.064 --> 01:07:51.192
Then you should've
cleared things up right there…

01:07:51.276 --> 01:07:52.819
I did!

01:07:52.902 --> 01:07:56.531
I said it was a misunderstanding
over and over, but you didn't listen.

01:07:57.156 --> 01:07:58.199
Forget it.

01:07:59.576 --> 01:08:03.162
I can't blame you.
You were just born that way.

01:08:04.497 --> 01:08:06.416
[soft tender music playing]

01:08:06.499 --> 01:08:08.918
Maybe I have a victim mentality,
like you said.

01:08:11.379 --> 01:08:16.759
Fine. I took your words
the wrong way. Happy?

01:08:19.178 --> 01:08:20.138
[sniffles]

01:08:38.156 --> 01:08:39.240
Are you asleep?

01:08:41.492 --> 01:08:42.619
Good night.

01:08:45.038 --> 01:08:46.372
[music fades]

01:08:46.456 --> 01:08:48.291
- Delivery!
- What the heck?

01:08:48.374 --> 01:08:49.959
Jeez.

01:08:50.585 --> 01:08:52.545
- [grunts]
- I didn't order anything.

01:08:53.546 --> 01:08:55.340
Yes, I lied. [chuckles]

01:08:55.923 --> 01:08:57.592
Hey. Wow.

01:08:58.426 --> 01:08:59.886
It's been a while.

01:09:02.305 --> 01:09:05.933
So, I heard you stood up for me
at the wedding?

01:09:06.851 --> 01:09:09.354
I wouldn't say that exactly.

01:09:09.896 --> 01:09:11.731
Whatever. Thanks anyway.

01:09:12.857 --> 01:09:18.738
Since you stood up for me,
I figured I should ask.

01:09:19.697 --> 01:09:21.616
Are you stringing Mi-ji along?

01:09:21.699 --> 01:09:24.410
- What?
- She doesn't have a proper job,

01:09:24.494 --> 01:09:26.913
and she's not educated like you.
Is that it?

01:09:26.996 --> 01:09:29.374
- Is she not good enough for you?
- Don't be ridiculous.

01:09:29.457 --> 01:09:30.708
Good.

01:09:30.792 --> 01:09:33.211
You're getting defensive and upset.

01:09:33.961 --> 01:09:36.172
But why won't you tell her?

01:09:36.839 --> 01:09:38.633
You've liked her since way back.

01:09:39.133 --> 01:09:40.843
The timing wasn't right back then.

01:09:41.886 --> 01:09:43.721
Just when I finally made up my mind…

01:09:45.139 --> 01:09:48.309
she was in a really bad place.

01:09:49.727 --> 01:09:51.062
[sighs heavily]

01:09:52.397 --> 01:09:53.856
So you couldn't tell her?

01:09:55.191 --> 01:09:56.067
[in English] Okay.

01:09:56.693 --> 01:09:58.069
[in Korean] What about now?

01:09:59.153 --> 01:10:00.863
We missed our chance once.

01:10:00.947 --> 01:10:03.116
[breathes deeply]

01:10:03.199 --> 01:10:07.078
This time, I want to do it right,
when nothing's in our way.

01:10:07.161 --> 01:10:08.996
Are you plotting an assassination?

01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:10.915
Do you need to plan out

01:10:10.998 --> 01:10:14.001
the exact spot, the route,
and even the exit strategy?

01:10:14.085 --> 01:10:15.378
[Ho-su] I'll do it later.

01:10:16.170 --> 01:10:18.005
She's uncomfortable around me now.

01:10:18.089 --> 01:10:19.716
When exactly is "later"?

01:10:21.676 --> 01:10:25.179
Fine. Just keep wasting time
and start dating when you're old and gray.

01:10:25.847 --> 01:10:28.683
You two are exactly the same.

01:10:29.767 --> 01:10:30.852
Ho-su.

01:10:31.644 --> 01:10:34.397
There's no such thing as perfect timing.

01:10:35.398 --> 01:10:37.233
Nothing in this world is perfect.

01:10:37.775 --> 01:10:40.278
[soft tender music playing]

01:10:50.163 --> 01:10:51.956
[soft tender music continues]

01:10:54.208 --> 01:10:56.669
"There's no such thing as perfect timing."

01:10:57.295 --> 01:10:58.963
- [music fades]
- [sighs contently]

01:11:00.506 --> 01:11:01.591
You killed it.

01:11:05.636 --> 01:11:08.264
RESIGNATION LETTER

01:11:08.347 --> 01:11:10.808
KFMC PLANNING STRATEGY TEAM
YU MI-RAE

01:11:13.978 --> 01:11:15.229
[Mi-rae] Weren't you scared?

01:11:16.647 --> 01:11:18.691
You worked so hard to get there,

01:11:19.317 --> 01:11:20.985
but you just gave it all up and left.

01:11:22.111 --> 01:11:23.321
I was terrified.

01:11:25.072 --> 01:11:28.409
But if you don't let go,
you can't grab onto anything else.

01:11:29.494 --> 01:11:32.330
So let's grab onto
any happiness, goodness,

01:11:33.331 --> 01:11:34.957
or joy we can find.

01:11:35.458 --> 01:11:36.501
You too, Mi-rae.

01:11:36.584 --> 01:11:38.252
[gentle music playing]

01:11:41.547 --> 01:11:43.216
[gentle music continues]

01:11:51.224 --> 01:11:53.434
RESIGNATION LETTER

01:12:00.107 --> 01:12:01.609
FOR THE REASONS STATED ABOVE,

01:12:01.692 --> 01:12:04.278
I HEREBY SUBMIT MY RESIGNATION

01:12:04.362 --> 01:12:06.697
SORRY I MADE YOU GO THROUGH THIS ALONE

01:12:07.532 --> 01:12:08.533
[Mi-ji sighs]

01:12:10.993 --> 01:12:12.245
NEW HQ PROJECT

01:12:12.328 --> 01:12:14.038
What do I do with this?

01:12:14.121 --> 01:12:15.540
[music fades]

01:12:15.623 --> 01:12:16.749
[sighs]

01:12:19.126 --> 01:12:20.670
[Mi-ji mutters, clicks tongue]

01:12:21.546 --> 01:12:24.006
- [knocking on wall]
- [Mi-rae] What are you doing?

01:12:24.090 --> 01:12:28.261
Just organizing things to tell you
before you go back to Seoul.

01:12:28.886 --> 01:12:29.971
Oh…

01:12:32.098 --> 01:12:33.391
Sorry, but…

01:12:33.474 --> 01:12:35.685
can we wait a few more days
before we switch back?

01:12:36.978 --> 01:12:38.354
It won't take long.

01:12:38.437 --> 01:12:41.232
I'll wrap things up here first
and go back right away.

01:12:41.315 --> 01:12:43.109
- Oh…
- [pages rustling]

01:12:43.192 --> 01:12:44.902
That's fine with me.

01:12:45.570 --> 01:12:47.822
But why? Is something going on?

01:12:57.748 --> 01:12:59.584
Remember what you said

01:13:00.751 --> 01:13:02.169
the first day we switched?

01:13:03.212 --> 01:13:06.966
You told me to write a resignation letter
when I was ready to come back.

01:13:09.719 --> 01:13:11.888
I said I would,

01:13:13.472 --> 01:13:15.766
but honestly,
I wasn't planning to write it.

01:13:17.560 --> 01:13:19.562
I never considered quitting.

01:13:20.938 --> 01:13:22.231
I was scared.

01:13:22.732 --> 01:13:24.400
- [gentle music playing]
- Of what?

01:13:25.067 --> 01:13:29.155
I feel like KFMC
is way more than I deserve.

01:13:29.238 --> 01:13:32.408
- Don't say that.
- [Mi-rae] I mean it.

01:13:33.034 --> 01:13:34.744
I was just lucky to get in.

01:13:35.953 --> 01:13:40.541
You and Mom always talk like
I'm some big deal,

01:13:41.167 --> 01:13:43.252
but I'm just average.

01:13:44.378 --> 01:13:47.214
I'm just good at enduring tedious stuff.

01:13:48.674 --> 01:13:50.968
If you just compare
the results to my effort,

01:13:51.719 --> 01:13:53.763
I might even be below average.

01:13:56.557 --> 01:13:58.726
That's why I was scared to quit.

01:14:00.603 --> 01:14:01.979
Getting into KFMC

01:14:03.147 --> 01:14:04.690
was just a stroke of luck

01:14:05.399 --> 01:14:07.109
for someone as average as me.

01:14:07.902 --> 01:14:12.573
Come on. You could get a job
at a much better place.

01:14:12.657 --> 01:14:14.325
For me, this company is…

01:14:15.952 --> 01:14:17.828
like what running was to you.

01:14:19.038 --> 01:14:21.874
I could go somewhere else,

01:14:22.917 --> 01:14:26.128
but I don't think I could go
anywhere better than KFMC.

01:14:28.005 --> 01:14:30.049
So I was scared to let it go.

01:14:31.884 --> 01:14:33.135
[Mi-rae sighs]

01:14:33.219 --> 01:14:35.763
If I leave, I have to start over.

01:14:36.722 --> 01:14:38.432
And I'm just tired…

01:14:39.809 --> 01:14:41.602
of being disappointed in myself.

01:14:42.353 --> 01:14:44.230
[Mi-rae breathes deeply]

01:14:44.313 --> 01:14:47.358
That's why it took me so long
to write a resignation letter

01:14:48.567 --> 01:14:50.069
that I might not even hand in.

01:14:51.904 --> 01:14:53.572
I must sound so pathetic.

01:14:54.615 --> 01:14:55.783
Hey.

01:14:56.575 --> 01:14:59.328
Either laugh or cry. Pick one.

01:15:00.037 --> 01:15:01.539
[chuckles, sniffles]

01:15:03.833 --> 01:15:05.793
[Mi-rae] I spent days in silence,

01:15:06.585 --> 01:15:10.047
keeping to myself
so no one would see how vulnerable I was.

01:15:11.048 --> 01:15:13.342
[music fades]

01:15:13.426 --> 01:15:15.261
[cell phone buzzing]

01:15:16.846 --> 01:15:18.556
[buzzing continues]

01:15:21.976 --> 01:15:23.310
[Ok-hui over phone] Hello.

01:15:26.022 --> 01:15:27.273
Ok-hui.

01:15:30.693 --> 01:15:32.069
Are you hurt?

01:15:33.988 --> 01:15:36.157
Does it hurt a lot?

01:15:37.199 --> 01:15:38.492
[Ok-hui] Mom, is that you?

01:15:40.036 --> 01:15:42.079
[soft tender music playing]

01:15:42.163 --> 01:15:43.497
I'm fine.

01:15:46.751 --> 01:15:47.710
[breathes deeply]

01:15:47.793 --> 01:15:49.128
[Ok-hui] I'm hanging up.

01:15:49.211 --> 01:15:50.629
[phone clicks]

01:15:50.713 --> 01:15:52.882
[disconnect tone beeping]

01:15:59.638 --> 01:16:01.182
Thank you.

01:16:06.479 --> 01:16:08.022
I'm sorry.

01:16:13.986 --> 01:16:17.114
KIM RO-SA

01:16:17.198 --> 01:16:19.325
[soft tender music continues]

01:16:21.368 --> 01:16:23.746
[Mi-rae]
Inside the layers of bark I've built up

01:16:24.747 --> 01:16:27.374
in my wish to become a tree…

01:16:31.045 --> 01:16:32.546
there are fragile feelings

01:16:33.255 --> 01:16:35.132
trapped within,

01:16:35.966 --> 01:16:37.343
unable to grow.

01:16:38.010 --> 01:16:39.970
[soft tender music continues]

01:16:53.651 --> 01:16:54.777
[door opens]

01:16:56.278 --> 01:16:58.280
[music fades]

01:17:00.699 --> 01:17:01.951
[gate opens]

01:17:02.034 --> 01:17:05.412
Ho-su. I just saw your text.

01:17:05.496 --> 01:17:07.456
What's up? It's late.

01:17:07.540 --> 01:17:10.000
Have you been waiting long?

01:17:10.960 --> 01:17:12.002
No.

01:17:12.086 --> 01:17:14.130
You're lying.

01:17:14.213 --> 01:17:16.090
Your face looks numb from the cold.

01:17:16.173 --> 01:17:18.175
Honestly, I've been waiting a long time.

01:17:19.593 --> 01:17:20.970
A very long time.

01:17:24.515 --> 01:17:25.850
Mi-ji.

01:17:28.602 --> 01:17:30.563
I've been thinking about that day…

01:17:32.106 --> 01:17:33.899
the whole time I was waiting.

01:17:35.276 --> 01:17:37.027
On the day before I left for Seoul,

01:17:37.820 --> 01:17:40.364
I was waiting for you here just like this.

01:17:41.490 --> 01:17:44.118
I had something I needed to say…
[inhales deeply]

01:17:45.411 --> 01:17:48.747
…but I couldn't say a word
when you came out.

01:17:48.831 --> 01:17:52.877
Back then, I was in a bad place,
and I took it out on you.

01:17:54.128 --> 01:17:56.964
When I was in a bad place,
you always reached out to me,

01:17:57.590 --> 01:17:59.175
even when I was mean.

01:18:00.050 --> 01:18:03.095
I wanted to be
that kind of person for you too.

01:18:04.680 --> 01:18:08.142
But seeing you struggle after your injury…

01:18:09.393 --> 01:18:11.520
[sighs] …I lost my courage.

01:18:13.772 --> 01:18:16.817
I don't have the strength
to help someone heal like you do.

01:18:16.901 --> 01:18:19.945
I thought I'd only end up
hurting you more.

01:18:21.906 --> 01:18:23.908
If I was never going to see you again,

01:18:25.326 --> 01:18:29.079
I thought I'd rather just say nothing
and keep things the way they were.

01:18:29.705 --> 01:18:32.625
It would have been enough
just to catch a glimpse of you

01:18:32.708 --> 01:18:34.585
on the day of the ancestral rite.

01:18:34.668 --> 01:18:35.961
Back then, at least.

01:18:39.215 --> 01:18:40.549
[breathes shakily]

01:18:40.633 --> 01:18:42.927
[tender music playing]

01:18:56.273 --> 01:18:57.358
[Ho-su] Mi-ji.

01:18:59.401 --> 01:19:01.487
I've been waiting to tell you this,

01:19:02.488 --> 01:19:04.281
waiting until your heart was lighter

01:19:04.365 --> 01:19:07.409
and I had become a better person.

01:19:10.537 --> 01:19:11.789
But I'll say it now.

01:19:16.168 --> 01:19:17.461
I've liked you…

01:19:19.922 --> 01:19:21.215
for a long time.

01:19:23.467 --> 01:19:24.885
More than you know.

01:19:27.388 --> 01:19:29.431
[music fades]

01:19:30.099 --> 01:19:32.017
[gentle pop song playing]

01:19:32.101 --> 01:19:38.023
[singing in Korean]

01:19:38.107 --> 01:19:43.153
[singing in Korean continues]

01:19:44.071 --> 01:19:49.952
[singing in Korean continues]

01:19:50.035 --> 01:19:55.207
[singing in Korean continues]

01:19:57.001 --> 01:20:00.879
[singing in Korean continues]

01:20:02.214 --> 01:20:06.010
[singing in Korean continues]

01:20:06.093 --> 01:20:08.679
[Se-jin] When are you going to Seoul?
If you're not leaving today,

01:20:08.762 --> 01:20:10.180
do you want to meet up tonight?

01:20:10.264 --> 01:20:11.515
[Mi-rae] Why at night?

01:20:11.598 --> 01:20:13.434
[Se-jin]
Because the stars are visible at night.

01:20:13.517 --> 01:20:15.769
Are you her son?
You're just as handsome as she said.

01:20:15.853 --> 01:20:18.814
- What was the conception dream?
- [Ho-su] Do you still feel uncomfortable?

01:20:18.897 --> 01:20:21.567
Mom, just focus
on taking care of yourself.

01:20:21.650 --> 01:20:23.277
[Ro-sa]
If you're not a customer, get out.

01:20:23.360 --> 01:20:26.030
- Hyeon Sang-wol. You know her, right?
- [Ro-sa] Who are you?

01:20:26.113 --> 01:20:27.323
Hello.

01:20:27.406 --> 01:20:29.491
- [employee 1] Sang-yeong!
- [employee 2] You're back!

01:20:29.575 --> 01:20:31.243
[employee 1] You're back already?

01:20:31.744 --> 01:20:33.329
[Sang-yeong] How have you been?

01:20:33.954 --> 01:20:39.710
- [song continues]
- [singing in Korean continues]

01:20:40.671 --> 01:20:42.671
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
